gin used to drop both.\n  - `system-spec-kit` (v2.12.41.0 to v2.13.2.0) has its own changelog entries for this release. So does `system-skill-advisor` (v0.18.6.0, v0.18.7.0 and v1.0.0.0). So do `system-skilled-doctor` (v1.1.3.0 \n  - - **If you match on an advisor command id:** `memory:save` and `command-memory-save` are now `command-speckit-save`. `command-spec-kit` is now one id per command, such as `command-speckit-plan`. `comm\n\n### 2427bc4c4b6 .skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md lost 9 lines from main-parent\n  - - **A typed slash command always reaches the model.** It arrives with its policy and the skill that owns it. <!-- section: Skill Advisor -->\n  - - **Doctor checks show whether the brief arrives.** `/doctor:setup` gains an embedder leg and a delivery leg. <!-- section: Skill Advisor -->\n  - The advisor used to say `sk-doc` for \"create a readme\". You then had to find `/create:readme` yourself. Now a hub recommendation carries the command for the mode it picked. A brief head reads `use sys\n  - A typed slash command now reaches the model on every tracked row, with its policy and owner skill. Plain requests reach their command more often too. Paraphrases the tuning never saw still mostly miss\n  - A command can also pass on meaning when the local embedder runs. Each scored command row carries its own vector. A prompt needs a close match and a clear lead over the next command. A prompt that asks\n  - `/doctor:setup` gains two read-only legs. The embedder leg reads DEGRADED when meaning matching is off. The delivery leg reads DEGRADED when a prompt hook is missing or not approved. On Codex, no brie\n  - - **An OpenCode brief names the command and its policy.** The plugin used to drop both.\n  - `system-spec-kit` (v2.12.41.0 to v2.13.2.0) has its own changelog entries for this release. So does `system-skill-advisor` (v0.18.6.0, v0.18.7.0 and v1.0.0.0). So do `system-skilled-doctor` (v1.1.3.0 \n  - - **If you match on an advisor command id:** `memory:s