{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794815855055,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e35c82bd002f1ixGU4qoAqG5V","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","messageID":"msg_1e35c554d001aoZYECcrSawzOJ","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3a3b4414f21ce53","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.4.0.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.4.0.md, lines 1-32\n1: ---\n2: title: \"system-spec-kit v2.13.4.0, no command file may be named skill.md\"\n3: description: \"v2.13.4.0 makes the runtime mirror check fail on any command file named skill.md, in any capitalisation, and gives /speckit:search four plain-word intent phrases.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"system-spec-kit v2.13.4.0\"\n6:   - \"system-spec-kit 2.13.4.0\"\n7:   - \"skill.md command file refused\"\n8:   - \"speckit search intent phrases\"\n9: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n10: contextType: \"general\"\n11: version: 2.13.4.0\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # v2.13.4.0, No Command File May Be Named skill.md\n15: \n16: Claude Code reads a command folder that holds `skill.md` as one skill. It then hides every other command in that folder. The mirror check used to allow one such file, `create/skill.md`. That command is now `/create:sk-skill`, so the check allows none.\n17: \n18: > Spec folder: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\n19: \n20: &nbsp;\n21: \n22: ## What's New at a Glance\n23: \n24: - **The mirror check fails on any command file named `skill.md`.** It matches every capitalisation, so `SKILL.md` fails too. The failure reads `COLLAPSE design/SKILL.md hides 1 sibling commands on Claude Code`.\n25: - **The mirror check keeps no allowlist.** The old exception for `create/skill.md` is gone.\n26: - **`/speckit:search` answers plain search requests.** It gained four intent phrases, such as \"search our spec notes for a topic\".\n27: \n28: &nbsp;\n29: \n30: ## Upgrade\n31: \n32: No migration required. Rename any command file named `skill.md` in your own command folders before you run the mirror sync.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.4.0.md, lines 1-32\n1: ---\n2: title: \"system-spec-kit v2.13.4.0, no command file may be named skill.md\"\n3: description: \"v2.13.4.0 makes the runtime mirror check fail on any command file named skill.md, in any capitalisation, and gives /speckit:search four plain-word intent phrases.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"system-spec-kit v2.13.4.0\"\n6:   - \"system-spec-kit 2.13.4.0\"\n7:   - \"skill.md command file refused\"\n8:   - \"speckit search intent phrases\"\n9: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n10: contextType: \"general\"\n11: version: 2.13.4.0\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # v2.13.4.0, No Command File May Be Named skill.md\n15: \n16: Claude Code reads a command folder that holds `skill.md` as one skill. It then hides every other command in that folder. The mirror check used to allow one such file, `create/skill.md`. That command is now `/create:sk-skill`, so the check allows none.\n17: \n18: > Spec folder: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\n19: \n20: &nbsp;\n21: \n22: ## What's New at a Glance\n23: \n24: - **The mirror check fails on any command file named `skill.md`.** It matches every capitalisation, so `SKILL.md` fails too. The failure reads `COLLAPSE design/SKILL.md hides 1 sibling commands on Claude Code`.\n25: - **The mirror check keeps no allowlist.** The old exception for `create/skill.md` is gone.\n26: - **`/speckit:search` answers plain search requests.** It gained four intent phrases, such as \"search our spec notes for a topic\".\n27: \n28: &nbsp;\n29: \n30: ## Upgrade\n31: \n32: No migration required. Rename any command file named `skill.md` in your own command folders before you run the mirror sync."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.4.0.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794815853245,"end":1794815855055}}}}
