{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794815929831,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","part":{"id":"prt_1e35dade7001TeZcSb7Qh326kc","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","messageID":"msg_1e35d990d001k5pQ508ccbk5d8","type":"step-start","snapshot":"e034f72620768c9f18eb8dba7c8d026d97c81944"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794815933454,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e35db263001DbY3VTA6sOriIm","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","messageID":"msg_1e35d990d001k5pQ508ccbk5d8","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae47c18d30ddd7ca","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\\|MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED\\|MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED\\|MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED\" .skilled/hooks/shared .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/env-aliases.ts 2>/dev/null | head -20; echo \"--- alias file\"; ls .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib | grep -i alias"},"output":".skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.sh:7:# ENABLED (return 0) unless master SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED (or legacy MK_HOOKS_DISABLED) or per-concern SYSTEM_<CONCERN>_DISABLED\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.sh:99:  for __hf_master in SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED MK_HOOKS_DISABLED; do\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:41:const MASTER_ALIASES = [\"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\"];\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:73:    \"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED\",\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:74:    \"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED\",\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:75:    \"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED\",\n.skilled/hooks/shared/README.md:23:**Kill-switch resolver.** `hook-flags.cjs` exports `isHookEnabled(concern, env?, config?)`: default-on, so adding the guard changes no behavior until a flag is set. A hook goes silent when the master switch (`SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED`, alias `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED`) or one of the concern's kill-switches is truthy (`1`/`true`/`yes`/`on`, case-insensitive). A short list of concerns is default-off instead, `DEFAULT_OFF` in `hook-flags.cjs`, and today it holds one entry: `session-handover`. A default-off concern answers enabled only when its enable flag is truthy, read from the same two sources as the kill-switches. For `session-handover` the caller names its runtime through a fourth `options.runtime` argument, and the enable flag is that runtime's `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_<RUNTIME>_ENABLED` (`CLAUDE`, `CODEX`, `PI`, `OPENCODE`, `CURSOR`, `DEVIN` or `VIBE`) when it holds a non-empty value, `1` on and `0` off, and `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED` when it holds a non-empty value. With both blank, a runtime that `DEFAULT_ON_RUNTIMES` lists for the concern is on, and today that is `claude` alone, so Claude Code hands over by default while every other runtime and a caller that names none stays off. Each key resolves environment first, then config file, before that rule applies, so a config-file `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_CLAUDE_ENABLED=0` beats an environment `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED=1` for Claude Code. The master switch and the concern's kill-switch still win over every enable flag. `concernFlag(concern)` derives the canonical env-var name: concerns listed in `CONCERN_CANONICAL` get their hand-set name (e.g. `goal` → `OPENCODE_GOAL_DISABLED`, `dispatch` → `CLI_DISPATCH_AUDIT_DISABLED`); every other concern falls back to the default shape `SYSTEM_<CONCERN>_DISABLED`. `LEGACY_ALIASES` maps each concern to the older `MK_`/`SPECKIT_`/plugin-owned names that also disable it, so operator config written against any generation keeps working. `isFlagOn(name, env?, config?)` answers the same question for one named switch that is not a hook concern, such as the `SPECKIT_SKIP_VALIDATION` and `SKDOC_SKIP_VALIDATION` validation switches: the environment answers whenever the name is set there, even to an empty value, and the config file answers otherwise.\n.skilled/hooks/shared/README.md:97:| `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED=1` | Legacy alias of the master switch. |\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs:104:  const names = [MASTER_FLAG, \"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\", \"SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED\", ...LEGACY_ALIASES[\"skill-advisor\"]];\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs:199:  const names = [MASTER_FLAG, \"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\", \"SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_DISABLED\", \"SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED\"];\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs:223:  assert.equal(isHookEnabled(\"session-handover\", { ...on, MK_HOOKS_DISABLED: \"1\" }), false);\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs:239:  const names = [MASTER_FLAG, \"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\", \"SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_DISABLED\", \"SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED\", \"SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED\"];\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs:317:  const names = [MASTER_FLAG, \"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\", \"OPENCODE_GOAL_DISABLED\", ...LEGACY_ALIASES.goal];\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs:354:      delete env.MK_HOOKS_DISABLED;\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs:453:    for (const name of [\"SKDOC_SKIP_VALIDATION\", \"SYSTEM_PROBE_DISABLED\", MASTER_FLAG, \"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\"]) delete env[name];\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs:553:    delete env.MK_HOOKS_DISABLED;\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs:585:      [\"the legacy master alias beats every opt-in\", { SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED: \"1\", SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_CLAUDE_ENABLED: \"1\", MK_HOOKS_DISABLED: \"1\" }, \"\", \"off off off off off\"],\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs:586:      [\"the legacy master alias in the file beats an environment opt-in\", { SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED: \"1\" }, \"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED=1\\n\", \"off off off off off\"],\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs:590:        if (/^SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_/.test(name) || name === MASTER_FLAG || name === \"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\") delete env[name];\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs:628:    if (/^SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_/.test(name) || name === MASTER_FLAG || name === \"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\") delete env[name];\n--- alias file\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":1},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.sh:7:# ENABLED (return 0) unless master SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED (or legacy MK_HOOKS_DISABLED) or per-concern SYSTEM_<CONCERN>_DISABLED\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.sh:99:  for __hf_master in SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED MK_HOOKS_DISABLED; do\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:41:const MASTER_ALIASES = [\"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\"];\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:73:    \"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED\",\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:74:    \"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED\",\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:75:    \"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED\",\n.skilled/hooks/shared/README.md:23:**Kill-switch resolver.** `hook-flags.cjs` exports `isHookEnabled(concern, env?, config?)`: default-on, so adding the guard changes no behavior until a flag is set. A hook goes silent when the master switch (`SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED`, alias `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED`) or one of the concern's kill-switches is truthy (`1`/`true`/`yes`/`on`, case-insensitive). A short list of concerns is default-off instead, `DEFAULT_OFF` in `hook-flags.cjs`, and today it holds one entry: `session-handover`. A default-off concern answers enabled only when its enable flag is truthy, read from the same two sources as the kill-switches. For `session-handover` the caller names its runtime through a fourth `options.runtime` argument, and the enable flag is that runtime's `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_<RUNTIME>_ENABLED` (`CLAUDE`, `CODEX`, `PI`, `OPENCODE`, `CURSOR`, `DEVIN` or `VIBE`) when it holds a non-empty value, `1` on and `0` off, and `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED` when it holds a non-empty value. With both blank, a runtime that `DEFAULT_ON_RUNTIMES` lists for the concern is on, and today that is `claude` alone, so Claude Code hands over by default while every other runtime and a caller that names none stays off. Each key resolves environment first, then config file, before that rule applies, so a config-file `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_CLAUDE_ENABLED=0` beats an environment `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED=1` for Claude Code. The master switch and the concern's kill-switch still win over every enable flag. `concernFlag(concern)` derives the canonical env-var name: concerns listed in `CONCERN_CANONICAL` get their hand-set name (e.g. `goal` → `OPENCODE_GOAL_DISABLED`, `dispatch` → `CLI_DISPATCH_AUDIT_DISABLED`); every other concern falls back to the default shape `SYSTEM_<CONCERN>_DISABLED`. `LEGACY_ALIASES` maps each concern to the older `MK_`/`SPECKIT_`/plugin-owned names that also disable it, so operator config written against any generation keeps working. `isFlagOn(name, env?, config?)` answers the same question for one named switch that is not a hook concern, such as the `SPECKIT_SKIP_VALIDATION` and `SKDOC_SKIP_VALIDATION` validation switches: the environment answers whenever the name is set there, even to an empty value, and the config file answers otherwise.\n.skilled/hooks/shared/README.md:97:| `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED=1` | Legacy alias of the master switch. |\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs:104:  const names = [MASTER_FLAG, \"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\", \"SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED\", ...LEGACY_ALIASES[\"skill-advisor\"]];\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs:199:  const names = [MASTER_FLAG, \"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\", \"SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_DISABLED\", \"SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED\"];\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs:223:  assert.equal(isHookEnabled(\"session-handover\", { ...on, MK_HOOKS_DISABLED: \"1\" }), false);\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs:239:  const names = [MASTER_FLAG, \"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\", \"SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_DISABLED\", \"SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED\", \"SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED\"];\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs:317:  const names = [MASTER_FLAG, \"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\", \"OPENCODE_GOAL_DISABLED\", ...LEGACY_ALIASES.goal];\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs:354:      delete env.MK_HOOKS_DISABLED;\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs:4