{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794815997854,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e35eb570001HmeRzY9xFG3P4y","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","messageID":"msg_1e35ea5cf001CmfJWRcOVQT2aI","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8cf5db09c08b902","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG\\|hook health\\|health record\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/*.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/references 2>/dev/null | head -20"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook-validation.md:100:Every hook run writes a prompt-free health record to the diagnostics sink, and `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1` adds the skill label and the error text to each record.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook-validation.md:103:export SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:514:      // The health record counts degraded answers, and only this step knows the\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:201:| Diagnostics | Each hook record carries `runtime` (the Codex, Cursor and Devin adapters set `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` and Pi passes `pi`) plus `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. Every prompt writes a health record to the diagnostics sink with no prompt, skill label or error text, and an answer from the CLI's local scorer carries `degraded: true`. `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` adds the skill label and the error text. The subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md:150:**Release validation.** `advisor_validate` runs the regression suite and reports threshold semantics (aggregate vs runtime) plus a prompt-safe `telemetry.outcomes.totals` block. Hook diagnostics persist to bounded JSONL sinks so `advisor_validate` can read them back across processes. Records carry the runtime that served the turn, the bytes delivered (`emittedBytes`) and whether the directives were suppressed (`directivesSuppressed`). Each hook run writes a health record with no prompt, skill label or error text, and `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` adds the skill label and the error text. The bounded trim writes a temp file and renames it over the log so a crash mid-trim keeps the old log.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook-validation.md:100:Every hook run writes a prompt-free health record to the diagnostics sink, and `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1` adds the skill label and the error text to each record.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook-validation.md:103:export SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:514:      // The health record counts degraded answers, and only this step knows the\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:201:| Diagnostics | Each hook record carries `runtime` (the Codex, Cursor and Devin adapters set `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` and Pi passes `pi`) plus `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. Every prompt writes a health record to the diagnostics sink with no prompt, skill label or error text, and an answer from the CLI's local scorer carries `degraded: true`. `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` adds the skill label and the error text. The subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md:150:**Release validation.** `advisor_validate` runs the regression suite and reports threshold semantics (aggregate vs runtime) plus a prompt-safe `telemetry.outcomes.totals` block. Hook diagnostics persist to bounded JSONL sinks so `advisor_validate` can read them back across processes. Records carry the runtime that served the turn, the bytes delivered (`emittedBytes`) and whether the directives were suppressed (`directivesSuppressed`). Each hook run writes a health record with no prompt, skill label or error text, and `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` adds the skill label and the error text. The bounded trim writes a temp file and renames it over the log so a crash mid-trim keeps the old log.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \\\"SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG\\\\|hook health\\\\|health record\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/*.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/references 2>/dev/null | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794815997296,"end":1794815997854}}}}
