{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794816041665,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e35f508c001Yax6QLBjPVdeGI","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","messageID":"msg_1e35f3f770011W3xDJ8AGk5WtN","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-952d053b9aa1f453","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rln \"SPECKIT_RUNTIME\" . --exclude-dir=node_modules --exclude-dir=specs --exclude-dir=.git --exclude-dir=dist 2>/dev/null | head -20; echo \"--- hook md\"; grep -n \"Codex\\|Cursor\\|Devin\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md | head -20"},"output":"./.skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs\n./.skilled/hooks/session-handover/tests/session-handover-cli.test.cjs\n./.skilled/hooks/session-handover/README.md\n./.skilled/hooks/session-handover/history/README.md\n./.skilled/hooks/session-handover/history/lib/lookup-offer.ts\n./.skilled/hooks/session-handover/history/lib/cli.ts\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.1.4.0.md\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hook-adapter-runtime-label.vitest.ts\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/env-reference-drift.vitest.ts\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/devin/shared.ts\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/devin/README.md\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/cursor/shared.ts\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/cursor/README.md\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/claude/hook-state.ts\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/codex/shared.ts\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/codex/README.md\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/plugins-and-hooks/compaction-history-lookup.md\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/compat/shim.vitest.ts\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/claude-user-prompt-submit-hook.vitest.ts\n--- hook md\n3:description: Operator contract for the maintained Skill Advisor adapters across Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi, DSH, Vibe and the OpenCode plugin. Surfaces a prompt-safe routing brief on each user prompt. Advisory only and fail-open.\n23:The maintained advisor implementation lives in `system-skill-advisor/runtime/`. The four editor runtimes (Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin) each carry a thin `user-prompt-submit` shim in `system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/<runtime>/` that resolves and spawns the compiled advisor in `system-skill-advisor`. The real brief-building, scoring, freshness, and rendering logic lives in the advisor package. Pi carries a native TypeScript extension that imports the same advisor module in-process (Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old two-process blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send). DSH carries a `repo-guards` adapter that imports the same compiled handler in-process. OpenCode integrates through the committed plugin at `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, which shells out to the advisor CLI.\n89:| **Codex** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.codex/hooks.json`, timeout 3s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope on resolution failure | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n90:| **Cursor** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.js` | `beforeSubmitPrompt` in `.cursor/hooks.json`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n91:| **Devin** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${DEVIN_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n106:| Codex | No | The mirror is a pointer stub that tells the model to read the command file. There is no `.codex/skills` |\n107:| Cursor | No model path found, and the brief is dormant | The mirror is a pointer stub. Public Cursor docs were not fetched |\n108:| Devin | No command surface at all | Skills are exposed, commands are not |\n201:| Diagnostics | Each hook record carries `runtime` (the Codex, Cursor and Devin adapters set `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` and Pi passes `pi`) plus `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. Every prompt writes a health record to the diagnostics sink with no prompt, skill label or error text, and an answer from the CLI's local scorer carries `degraded: true`. `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` adds the skill label and the error text. The subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit. |\n258:This compares the repository's maintained Codex registration and adapter paths. A report about the user-global installation is workstation state, not a repository defect.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"./.skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs\n./.skilled/hooks/session-handover/tests/session-handover-cli.test.cjs\n./.skilled/hooks/session-handover/README.md\n./.skilled/hooks/session-handover/history/README.md\n./.skilled/hooks/session-handover/history/lib/lookup-offer.ts\n./.skilled/hooks/session-handover/history/lib/cli.ts\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.1.4.0.md\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hook-adapter-runtime-label.vitest.ts\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/env-reference-drift.vitest.ts\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/devin/shared.ts\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/devin/README.md\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/cursor/shared.ts\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/cursor/README.md\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/claude/hook-state.ts\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/codex/shared.ts\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/codex/README.md\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/plugins-and-hooks/compaction-history-lookup.md\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/compat/shim.vitest.ts\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/claude-user-prompt-submit-hook.vitest.ts\n--- hook md\n3:description: Operator contract for the maintained Skill Advisor adapters across Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi, DSH, Vibe and the OpenCode plugin. Surfaces a prompt-safe routing brief on each user prompt. Advisory only and fail-open.\n23:The maintained advisor implementation lives in `system-skill-advisor/runtime/`. The four editor runtimes (Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin) each carry a thin `user-prompt-submit` shim in `system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/<runtime>/` that resolves and spawns the compiled advisor in `system-skill-advisor`. The real brief-building, scoring, freshness, and rendering logic lives in the advisor package. Pi carries a native TypeScript extension that imports the same advisor module in-process (Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old two-process blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send). DSH carries a `repo-guards` adapter that imports the same compiled handler in-process. OpenCode integrates through the committed plugin at `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, which shells out to the advisor CLI.\n89:| **Codex** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.codex/hooks.json`, timeout 3s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope on resolution failure | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n90:| **Cursor** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.js` | `beforeSubmitPrompt` in `.cursor/hooks.json`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n91:| **Devin** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${DEVIN_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n106:| Codex | No | The mirror is a pointer stub that tells the model to read the command file. There is no `.codex/skills` |\n107:| Cursor | No model path found, and the brief is dormant | The mirror is a pointer stub. Public Cursor docs were not fetched |\n108:| Devin | No command surface at all | Skills are exposed, commands are not |\n201:| Diagnostics | Each hook record carries `runtime` (the Codex, Cursor and Devin adapters set `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` and Pi passes `pi`) plus `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. Every prompt writes a health record to the diagnostics sink with no prompt, skill label or error text, and an answer from the CLI's local scorer carries `degraded: true`. `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` adds the skill label and the error text. The subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit. |\n258:This compares the repository's maintained Codex registration and adapter paths. A report about the user-global installation is workstation state, not a repository defect.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rln \\\"SPECKIT_RUNTIME\\\" . --exclude-dir=node_modules --exclude-dir=specs --exclude-dir=.git --exclude-dir=dist 2>/dev/null | head -20; echo \\\"--- hook md\\\"; grep -n \\\"Codex\\\\|Cursor\\\\|Devin\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794816037004,"end":1794816041665}}}}
