{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794816171520,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","part":{"id":"prt_1e3615e00001poRelHP8YYyBLN","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","messageID":"msg_1e3614fdb001yIkPhOTlYyRBLp","type":"step-start","snapshot":"a9aac2814524cc2d55960cd9eb70bc743ac9acae"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794816181039,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e3617a0d002LdISuEv15AYK9S","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","messageID":"msg_1e3614fdb001yIkPhOTlYyRBLp","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5d9f95a4967a32d","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":60,"path":".skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md, lines 1-60\n1: ---\n2: title: \"v4.0.2.1, Improved Chat Automation, Search & Session Handover\"\n3: description: \"Skilled now needs a patched Node.js, keeps .env values away from agents on all eight runtimes and names the command behind each hub skill. A session hop carries its command and goal, and search says what it left out.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"v4.0.2.1 release notes\"\n6:   - \"skilled v4.0.2.1\"\n7:   - \"dotenv secret guard\"\n8:   - \"patched node releases required\"\n9:   - \"hub skill names its command\"\n10:   - \"goal carried across a hop\"\n11:   - \"lookup reports total candidates\"\n12:   - \"strict overlay writes\"\n13: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n14: contextType: \"general\"\n15: ---\n16: # v4.0.2.1, Improved Chat Automation, Search & Session Handover\n17: \n18: This release changes what you install, what an agent may read and what it is told to run. Skilled now needs a patched Node.js release. A new guard keeps the values in a `.env` file away from every agent. The skill advisor now names the slash command behind a hub skill. It also says whether the agent may run it.\n19: \n20: Long sessions hand over more cleanly, and Claude Code now does it by default. Pi and OpenCode now finish a hop too, and so does Mistral Vibe. The feature now has one main name, session handover. A hop to a fresh session carries the running command, the goal and the session's name and mode. The shell shim trusts only your own checkout. Search answers now say how much they left out. A new spec document is found before the index catches up. The spec commands now save the continuity they report.\n21: \n22: Projects that vendor Skilled get stricter overlay checks and an engine that cleans up after itself. Pi 1.5.2 loads every hook adapter again. A plain frontend request now reaches the code skill's frontend guidance. Skilled's own checks and tests also run faster.\n23: \n24: Deep loops now stop on a decision a script computes. Each deep command runs from one workflow file. The AI Council leaves Deep Loop and becomes its own agent. A deep review now fails while a required check still fails at its stop. Scripts now compute those checks and the verdict. The agent files now ask only for steps their own tools can take.\n25: \n26: > Spec folders: `specs/system-speckit/repo-operations/004-node-security-patch-update`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/hook-injection-pipeline/007-env-secret-guard`, `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/036-review-remediation`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/037-relaunch-test-speed`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/038-goal-and-workflow-resume`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/039-hop-dialog-goal-title`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/040-claude-default-on-release-notes`, `specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers`, `specs/cli-external-orchestration/opencode-platform/004-self-invocation-guard-api-key`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/retrieval-integrations/001-sweet-search-integration`, `specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/005-goldfish-cold-read-plan-review`, `specs/agents-md/repo-rule-operations/005-reply-rule-pruning`, `specs/system-skilled-doctor/001-skill-and-overlay-build/008-overlay-first-write-checks`, `specs/system-skilled-doctor/001-skill-and-overlay-build/009-overlay-write-checks-follow-up`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/hook-platform/006-file-relative-adapter-imports`, `specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed`, `specs/system-speckit/repo-operations/005-main-ci-red-checks` and `specs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/002-named-subtracks-and-host-repos`, `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/009-git-history-lift`, `specs/sk-doc/doc-validation-tooling/005-router-empty-block-capture`, `specs/sk-doc/hub-routing-and-surfaces/006-compiled-route-rule-growth`, `specs/system-skill-advisor/runtime-lifecycle/006-advisor-native-node-resolution`, `specs/sk-doc/hub-routing-and-surfaces/007... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n27: \n28: &nbsp;\n29: \n30: ## Why This Release\n31: \n32: Some gaps put your project at risk. A security notice in October patched Node.js. Skilled still accepted Node 20. Any agent could read `.env` and send every secret in it to the model.\n33: \n34: Other gaps cost your agent time. A recommendation said `sk-doc` when you asked for a README. The agent then had to find `/create:readme` on its own. A search cut at its limit never said what it hid. A session that hopped mid-command came back as a plain chat and lost its place. And handover shipped off everywhere, so most Claude Code users never had it. Pi and OpenCode did not finish a hop in a live test either. The switches still said relaunch, while the docs said handover. A spec command reported a save that never wrote a line. A deep loop left its stop call to the model running it. Two runs on the same state could stop differently. A deep review could pass while a required check failed. The model running it judged those checks. The coverage check could not read what reviews recorded. Several agent files asked for steps their own tools could not take.\n35: \n36: &nbsp;\n37: \n38: ## What's New at a Glance\n39: \n40: - **Install a patched Node.js first.** Node 20, 23 and 25 are no longer accepted. <!-- section: Node.js -->\n41: - **An agent can no longer read or write `.env`.** It gets key names, parse errors and fingerprints instead, on all eight runtimes. <!-- section: Dotenv Guard -->\n42: - **A hub skill names the command to type.** The brief also says whether to run it, start it or ask first. <!-- section: Skill Advisor -->\n43: - **A typed slash command always reaches the model.** It arrives with its policy and the skill that owns it. **Breaking:** `/create:skill` is now `/create:sk-skill`, with no alias. <!-- section: Skill Advisor -->\n44: - **Doctor checks show whether the brief arrives.** `/doctor:setup` gains an embedder leg and a delivery leg. Hook health shows with no debug flag. <!-- section: Skill Advisor -->\n45: - **Claude Code hands over by default.** A hop keeps the running command, the goal, the session's name and its mode. The other runtimes stay off until you turn them on. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n46: - **The shell shim runs only a wrapper it trusts.** A cloned repository can no longer supply the script your shell runs. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n47: - **One main name now covers the whole feature.** The hook folder, the switches, the seed and the docs say session handover. The in-session spelling still works for the on and off switches. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n48: - **Old switch names are no longer read.** Rename each one. Move any open handoff note to the new folder. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n49: - **Pi and OpenCode now finish a hop.** Both complete the same hop as Claude Code, with no input from you. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n50: - **Mistral Vibe hands over on its own.** Turn on its switch and a Vibe session near its compaction point starts a fresh one, like Claude Code. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n51: - **A search says what it left out.** Lookups report their total. Free-text search shows one row per file. <!-- section: Search -->\n52: - **A new spec document is found at once.** A lookup with no hits reads the documents the index does not list yet. <!-- section: Search -->\n53: - **Agents reread your request before they say done.** The restraint check now runs when a spec adds scope. <!-- section: Spec Workflow -->\n54: - **Spec commands save what they say they save.** Their checks, review step and resume now match each command's own words. <!-- section: Spec Workflow -->\n55: - **Deep loops stop the same way every time.** A script makes the stop call. Each command runs from one workflow file. <!-- section: Deep Loop -->\n56: - **The AI Council is its own agent.** `/deep:ai-council` is gone. Run `/speckit:ai-council` instead. <!-- section: Deep Loop -->\n57: - **A deep review fails while a required check still fails.** Evidence, scope and coverage now count at the stop. Scripts compute them and the verdict. <!-- section: Deep Loop -->\n58: - **Agents ask only for what their tools can do.** The orchestrator sends deep work to its command. Each agent has a way to finish that it can take. <!-- section: Agents -->\n59: - **A plain frontend request reaches the code skill's frontend mode.** The code skill's keyword copies and documents now agree with its router. <!-- section: Code Skill -->\n60: - **A vendored tree can refuse writes no overlay owns.** The overlay engine also clears its own leftovers. <!-- section: Installs and Overlays -->\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 61]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md, lines 1-60\n1: ---\n2: title: \"v4.0.2.1, Improved Chat Automation, Search & Session Handover\"\n3: description: \"Skilled now needs a patched Node.js, keeps .env values away from agents on all eight runtimes and names the command behind each hub skill. A session hop carries its command and goal, and search says what it left out.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"v4.0.2.1 release notes\"\n6:   - \"skilled v4.0.2.1\"\n7:   - \"dotenv secret guard\"\n8:   - \"patched node releases required\"\n9:   - \"hub skill names its command\"\n10:   - \"goal carried across a hop\"\n11:   - \"lookup reports total candidates\"\n12:   - \"strict overlay writes\"\n13: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n14: contextType: \"general\"\n15: ---\n16: # v4.0.2.1, Improved Chat Automation, Search & Session Handover\n17: \n18: This release changes what you install, what an agent may read and what it is told to run. Skilled now needs a patched Node.js release. A new guard keeps the values in a `.env` file away from every agent. The skill advisor now names the slash command behind a hub skill. It also says whether the agent may run it.\n19: \n20: Long sessions hand over more cleanly, and Claude Code now does it by default. Pi and OpenCode now finish a hop too, and so does Mistral Vibe. The feature now has one main name, session handover. A hop to a fresh session carries the running command, the goal and the session's name and mode. The shell shim trusts only your own checkout. Search answers now say how much they left out. A new spec document is found before the index catches up. The spec commands now save the continuity they report.\n21: \n22: Projects that vendor Skilled get stricter overlay checks and an engine that cleans up after itself. Pi 1.5.2 loads every hook adapter again. A plain frontend request now reaches the code skill's frontend guidance. Skilled's own checks and tests also run faster.\n23: \n24: Deep loops now stop on a decision a script computes. Each deep command runs from one workflow file. The AI Council leaves Deep Loop and becomes its own agent. A deep review now fails while a required check still fails at its stop. Scripts now compute those checks and the verdict. The agent files now ask only for steps their own tools can take.\n25: \n26: > Spec folders: `specs/system-speckit/repo-operations/004-node-security-patch-update`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/hook-injection-pipeline/007-env-secret-guard`, `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/036-review-remediation`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/037-relaunch-test-speed`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/038-goal-and-workflow-resume`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/039-hop-dialog-goal-title`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/040-claude-default-on-release-notes`, `specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers`, `specs/cli-external-orchestration/opencode-platform/004-self-invocation-guard-api-key`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/retrieval-integrations/001-sweet-search-integration`, `specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/005-goldfish-cold-read-plan-review`, `specs/agents-md/repo-rule-operations/005-reply-rule-pruning`, `specs/system-skilled-doctor/001-skill-and-overlay-build/008-overlay-first-write-checks`, `specs/system-skilled-doctor/001-skill-and-overlay-build/009-overlay-write-checks-follow-up`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/hook-platform/006-file-relative-adapter-imports`, `specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed`, `specs/system-speckit/repo-operations/005-main-ci-red-checks` and `specs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/002-named-subtracks-and-host-repos`, `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/009-git-history-lift`, `specs/sk-doc/doc-validation-tooling/005-router-empty-block-capture`, `specs/sk-doc/hub-routing-and-surfaces/006-compiled-route-rule-growth`, `specs/system-skill-advisor/runtime-lifecycle/006-advisor-native-node-resolution`, `specs/sk-doc/hub-routing-and-surfaces/007... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n27: \n28: &nbsp;\n29: \n30: ## Why This Release\n31: \n32: Some gaps put your project at risk. A security notice in October patched Node.js. Skilled still accepted Node 20. Any agent could read `.env` and send every secret in it to the model.\n33: \n34: Other gaps cost your agent time. A recommendation said `sk-doc` when you asked for a README. The agent then had to find `/create:readme` on its own. A search cut at its limit never said what it hid. A session that hopped mid-command came back as a plain chat and lost its place. And handover shipped off everywhere, so most Claude Code users never had it. Pi and OpenCode did not finish a hop in a live test either. The switches still said relaunch, while the docs said handover. A spec command reported a save that never wrote a line. A deep loop left its stop call to the model running it. Two runs on the same state could stop differently. A deep review could pass while a required check failed. The model running it judged those checks. The coverage check could not read what reviews recorded. Several agent files asked for steps their own tools could not take.\n35: \n36: &nbsp;\n37: \n38: ## What's New at a Glance\n39: \n40: - **Install a patched Node.js first.** Node 20, 23 and 25 are no longer accepted. <!-- section: Node.js -->\n41: - **An agent can no longer read or write `.env`.** It gets key names, parse errors and fingerprints instead, on all eight runtimes. <!-- section: Dotenv Guard -->\n42: - **A hub skill names the command to type.** The brief also says whether to run it, start it or ask first. <!-- section: Skill Advisor -->\n43: - **A typed slash command always reaches the model.** It arrives with its policy and the skill that owns it. **Breaking:** `/create:skill` is now `/create:sk-skill`, with no alias. <!-- section: Skill Advisor -->\n44: - **Doctor checks show whether the brief arrives.** `/doctor:setup` gains an embedder leg and a delivery leg. Hook health shows with no debug flag. <!-- section: Skill Advisor -->\n45: - **Claude Code hands over by default.** A hop keeps the running command, the goal, the session's name and its mode. The other runtimes stay off until you turn them on. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n46: - **The shell shim runs only a wrapper it trusts.** A cloned repository can no longer supply the script your shell runs. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n47: - **One main name now covers the whole feature.** The hook folder, the switches, the seed and the docs say session handover. The in-session spelling still works for the on and off switches. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n48: - **Old switch names are no longer read.** Rename each one. Move any open handoff note to the new folder. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n49: - **Pi and OpenCode now finish a hop.** Both complete the same hop as Claude Code, with no input from you. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n50: - **Mistral Vibe hands over on its own.** Turn on its switch and a Vibe session near its compaction point starts a fresh one, like Claude Code. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n51: - **A search says what it left out.** Lookups report their total. Free-text search shows one row per file. <!-- section: Search -->\n52: - **A new spec document is found at once.** A lookup with no hits reads the documents the index does not list yet. <!-- section: Search -->\n53: - **Agents reread your request before they say done.** The restraint check now runs when a spec adds scope. <!-- section: Spec Workflow -->\n54: - **Spec commands save what they say they save.** Their checks, review step and resume now match each command's own words. <!-- section: Spec Workflow -->\n55: - **Deep loops stop the same way every time.** A script makes the stop call. Each command runs from one workflow file. <!-- section: Deep Loop -->\n56: - **The AI Council is its own agent.** `/deep:ai-council` is gone. Run `/speckit:ai-council` instead. <!-- section: Deep Loop -->\n57: - **A deep review fails while a required check still fails.** Evidence, scope and coverage now count at the stop. Scripts compute them and the verdict. <!-- section: Deep Loop -->\n58: - **Agents ask only for what their tools can do.** The orchestrator sends deep work to its command. Each agent has a way to finish that it can take. <!-- section: Agents -->\n59: - **A plain frontend request reaches the code skill's frontend mode.** The code skill's keyword copies and documents now agree with its router. <!-- section: Code Skill -->\n60: - **A vendored tree can refuse writes no overlay owns.** The overlay engine also clears its own leftovers. <!-- section: Installs and Overlays -->\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 61]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\": 60, \"path\": \".skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794816178701,"end":1794816181039}}}}
