{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794816226053,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e3622ff80019eHwELFzAbonyx","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","messageID":"msg_1e36219a2001Yzsd05NWfx6B7W","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfeed368823b60be","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"2.13.3.0\\|2.13.4.0\" README.md .skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.4.0.md | head -20"},"output":".skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md:480:`system-spec-kit` (v2.12.41.0 to v2.13.3.0) has its own changelog entries for this release. So does `system-skill-advisor` (v0.18.6.0, v0.18.7.0, v1.0.0.0 and v1.1.0.0). So do `system-skilled-doctor` (v1.1.3.0 to v1.1.7.0) and `system-deep-loop` (v1.6.24.0 to v2.0.2.0). Its modes `deep-research` (v1.15.13.0 to v1.15.15.0) and `deep-review` (v1.11.15.0 to v1.11.17.0) have entries. `cli-external-orchestration` (v2.0.0.0) and its modes `cli-opencode` (v1.5.10.0 to v1.5.12.0) and `cli-deepseek-harness` (v1.0.1.0 and v1.0.2.0) have entries too. So does `sk-doc` (v2.9.8.0 to v2.10.0.0). Its modes `sk-create-benchmark` (v1.6.7.0), `sk-create-changelog` (v1.5.0.0 to v1.5.2.0) and `sk-create-feature-catalog` (v1.0.12.0) have entries. So do `sk-create-manual-testing-playbook` (v1.1.2.0) and `sk-create-readme` (v1.3.15.0 and v1.3.16.0). So do `sk-create-repo-rule` (v1.1.8.0) and `sk-create-skill` (v1.16.0.0). So does `sk-create-agent` (v1.0.8.0 to v1.0.10.0). So does `sk-prompt` (v4.0.5.0). `sk-code` (v3.11.5.0 to v3.12.1.0) has entries. So do its modes `sk-code-quality` (v1.13.19.0 to v1.13.21.0) and `sk-code-review` (v1.9.17.0 and v1.9.18.0). So do `sk-code-skilled` (v2.2.0.0 to v2.2.2.0), `sk-code-frontend` (v1.2.0.0) and `sk-code-ci` (v1.1.16.0 and v1.1.17.0). So does `mcp-code-mode` (v1.0.18.0). `mcp-tooling` (v1.9.9.0 to v1.9.16.0) has entries. So does its mode `mcp-click-up` (v1.2.17.0 to v1.2.23.0). Its modes `mcp-chrome-devtools` (v1.0.24.0), `mcp-aside-devtools` (v1.1.10.0) and `mcp-figma` (v1.2.3.0) have entries too.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md:5:version: 2.13.4.0\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.4.0.md:2:title: \"system-spec-kit v2.13.4.0, no command file may be named skill.md\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.4.0.md:3:description: \"v2.13.4.0 makes the runtime mirror check fail on any command file named skill.md, in any capitalisation, and gives /speckit:search four plain-word intent phrases.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.4.0.md:5:  - \"system-spec-kit v2.13.4.0\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.4.0.md:6:  - \"system-spec-kit 2.13.4.0\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.4.0.md:11:version: 2.13.4.0\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.4.0.md:14:# v2.13.4.0, No Command File May Be Named skill.md\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md:480:`system-spec-kit` (v2.12.41.0 to v2.13.3.0) has its own changelog entries for this release. So does `system-skill-advisor` (v0.18.6.0, v0.18.7.0, v1.0.0.0 and v1.1.0.0). So do `system-skilled-doctor` (v1.1.3.0 to v1.1.7.0) and `system-deep-loop` (v1.6.24.0 to v2.0.2.0). Its modes `deep-research` (v1.15.13.0 to v1.15.15.0) and `deep-review` (v1.11.15.0 to v1.11.17.0) have entries. `cli-external-orchestration` (v2.0.0.0) and its modes `cli-opencode` (v1.5.10.0 to v1.5.12.0) and `cli-deepseek-harness` (v1.0.1.0 and v1.0.2.0) have entries too. So does `sk-doc` (v2.9.8.0 to v2.10.0.0). Its modes `sk-create-benchmark` (v1.6.7.0), `sk-create-changelog` (v1.5.0.0 to v1.5.2.0) and `sk-create-feature-catalog` (v1.0.12.0) have entries. So do `sk-create-manual-testing-playbook` (v1.1.2.0) and `sk-create-readme` (v1.