 michelkerkmeester  staff   96 Nov 12 10:24 design\n---\n--- vibe\n/create:skill-parent\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && ls -la .devin/agents/ 2>/dev/null | head; echo \\\"---\\\"; grep -rn \\\"/create:skill\\\\b\\\" .devin/agents 2>/dev/null | grep -v \\\"skill-parent\\\" | head; echo \\\"--- vibe\\\"; grep -o \\\"/create:skill[a-z-]*\\\" .vibe/agents/markdown.toml | sort -u\"}"},"time":{"start":1794816360369,"end":1794816362289}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794816365440,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e364442e001YgmHA7t6b7CA11","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","messageID":"msg_1e3642cc8001T9HGWbIdMFT7Ru","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1c90e7c0fb66c27","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn '`/create:skill`' . --exclude-dir=node_modules --exclude-dir=specs --exclude-dir=.git --exclude-dir=z_archive --exclude-dir=dist 2>/dev/null | head -20"},"output":"./.skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog/v2.10.0.0.md:3:description: \"v2.10.0.0 renames `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime with no alias, so no command file is named `skill.md` and Claude Code lists all 44 tracked commands.\"\n./.skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog/v2.10.0.0.md:16:`/create:skill` is now `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime, with no alias. The old file name caused the bug. A command file named `skill.md` makes Claude Code read its folder as one skill. Every other command in that folder disappears from the listing.\n./.skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog/v2.10.0.0.md:34:- **The command is now `/create:sk-skill`.** The typed, plain and slash variants all reach it. No command file has the old name. The skill advisor reads a typed `/create:skill` as `/create:sk-skill`. <!-- section: Create Skill Command -->\n./.skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog/v2.10.0.0.md:46:`/create:sk-skill` replaces `/create:skill` in the command file, its three assets, the two command catalogs and the sk-doc hub metadata. The command behaves as before. Only the name a reader types changed. The mode id, the packet folder and the `create-skill-*` asset file names keep their old spelling.\n./.skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog/v2.10.0.0.md:50:**Breaking:** No command file answers to `/create:skill` now. The skill advisor reads a typed `/create:skill` as `/create:sk-skill`. Any script, saved prompt or doc that still names it needs the new spelling. There is no alias to fall back on.\n./.skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog/v2.10.0.0.md:88:- **Scripts and docs that type `/create:skill`:** change them to `/create:sk-skill`. No command file answers to the old name. The skill advisor reads it as `/create:sk-skill`.\n./.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.6.0.0.md:28:- **`/create:skill` now blocks on the shape.** Its completion gate runs `validate_skill_package.py --strict`. So a routing-shape finding blocks creation. It does not print as a warning. The hub scaffold also keeps the compiled-routing directive in its final `## MACHINE ROUTER` section. That section is now numbered.\n\n[showing lines 14-20 of 20; full output saved to /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/opencode/shell/4c10847297631c3af43d766cf1908920fe00c449/sh_1e3644706002MKMzSZbMVVkNCv.out]","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":true,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"./.skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog/v2.10.0.0.md:3:description: \"v2.10.0.0 renames `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime with no alias, so no command file is named `skill.md` and Claude Code lists all 44 tracked commands.\"\n./.skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog/v2.10.0.0.md:16:`/create:skill` is now `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime, with no alias. The old file name caused the bug. A command file named `skill.md` makes Claude Code read its folder as one skill. Every other command in that folder disappears from the listing.\n./.skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog/v2.10.0.0.md:34:- **The command is now `/create:sk-skill`.** The typed, plain and slash variants all reach it. No command file has the old name. The skill advisor reads a typed `/create:skill` as `/create:sk-skill`. <!-- section: Create Skill Command -->\n./.skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog/v2.10.0.0.md:46:`/create:sk-skill` replaces `/create:skill` in the command file, its three assets, the two command catalogs and the sk-doc hub metadata. The command behaves as before. Only the name a reader types changed. The mode id, the packet folder and the `create-skill-*` asset file names keep their old spelling.\n./.skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog/v2.10.0.0.md:50:**Breaking:** No command file answers to `/create:skill` now. The skill advisor reads a typed `/create:skill` as `/create:sk-skill`. Any script, saved prompt or doc that still names it needs the new spelling. There is no alias to fall back on.\n./.skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog/v2.10.0.0.md:88:- **Scripts and docs that type `/create:skill`:** change them to `/create:sk-skill`. No command file answers to the old name. The skill advisor reads it as `/create:sk-skill`.\n./.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.6.0.0.md:28:- **`/create:skill` now blocks on the shape.** Its completion gate runs `validate_skill_package.py --strict`. So a routing-shape finding blocks creation. It does not print as a warning. The hub scaffold also keeps the compiled-routing directive in its final `## MACHINE ROUTER` section. That section is now numbered.\n\n[showing lines 14-20 of 20; full output saved to /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/opencode/shell/4c10847297631c3af43d766cf1908920fe00c449/sh_1e3644706002MKMzSZbMVVkNCv.out]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn '`/create:skill`' . --exclude-dir=node_modules --exclude-dir=specs --exclude-dir=.git --exclude-dir=z_archive --exclude-dir=dist 2>/dev/null | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794816361518,"end":1794816365440}}}}
