{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794816422126,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e3652002002TSoS7wQZ5A9JmZ","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","messageID":"msg_1e364fcc1001YgOFU2FTmBzZ1B","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd23c902e54b2459","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"2\\.13\\.3\\.0\" . --exclude-dir=node_modules --exclude-dir=specs --exclude-dir=.git --exclude-dir=z_archive 2>/dev/null | head -20"},"output":"./.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md:480:`system-spec-kit` (v2.12.41.0 to v2.13.3.0) has its own changelog entries for this release. So does `system-skill-advisor` (v0.18.6.0, v0.18.7.0, v1.0.0.0 and v1.1.0.0). So do `system-skilled-doctor` (v1.1.3.0 to v1.1.7.0) and `system-deep-loop` (v1.6.24.0 to v2.0.2.0). Its modes `deep-research` (v1.15.13.0 to v1.15.15.0) and `deep-review` (v1.11.15.0 to v1.11.17.0) have entries. `cli-external-orchestration` (v2.0.0.0) and its modes `cli-opencode` (v1.5.10.0 to v1.5.12.0) and `cli-deepseek-harness` (v1.0.1.0 and v1.0.2.0) have entries too. So does `sk-doc` (v2.9.8.0 to v2.10.0.0). Its modes `sk-create-benchmark` (v1.6.7.0), `sk-create-changelog` (v1.5.0.0 to v1.5.2.0) and `sk-create-feature-catalog` (v1.0.12.0) have entries. So do `sk-create-manual-testing-playbook` (v1.1.2.0) and `sk-create-readme` (v1.3.15.0 and v1.3.16.0). So do `sk-create-repo-rule` (v1.1.8.0) and `sk-create-skill` (v1.16.0.0). So does `sk-create-agent` (v1.0.8.0 to v1.0.10.0). So does `sk-prompt` (v4.0.5.0). `sk-code` (v3.11.5.0 to v3.12.1.0) has entries. So do its modes `sk-code-quality` (v1.13.19.0 to v1.13.21.0) and `sk-code-review` (v1.9.17.0 and v1.9.18.0). So do `sk-code-skilled` (v2.2.0.0 to v2.2.2.0), `sk-code-frontend` (v1.2.0.0) and `sk-code-ci` (v1.1.16.0 and v1.1.17.0). So does `mcp-code-mode` (v1.0.18.0). `mcp-tooling` (v1.9.9.0 to v1.9.16.0) has entries. So does its mode `mcp-click-up` (v1.2.17.0 to v1.2.23.0). Its modes `mcp-chrome-devtools` (v1.0.24.0), `mcp-aside-devtools` (v1.1.10.0) and `mcp-figma` (v1.2.3.0) have entries too.\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.3.0.md:2:title: \"system-spec-kit v2.13.3.0, the nested changelog generator is removed\"\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.3.0.md:3:description: \"v2.13.3.0 removes the deprecated nested changelog generator, its test, its templates and its docs. The packet changelogs already written stay as history.\"\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.3.0.md:5:  - \"system-spec-kit v2.13.3.0\"\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.3.0.md:6:  - \"system-spec-kit 2.13.3.0\"\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.3.0.md:10:version: 2.13.3.0\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.3.0.md:13:# v2.13.3.0, The Nested Changelog Generator Is Removed\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures/phrase-variants.json:123943:      \"system-spec-kit 2.13.3.0\"\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures/phrase-variants.json:124600:      \"system-spec-kit v2.13.3.0\"\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures/corpus-manifest.json:8727:    \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.3.0.md\",\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/data/trigger-index.json:3127:    \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.3.0.md\",\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"./.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md:480:`system-spec-kit` (v2.12.41.0 to v2.13.3.0) has its own changelog entries for this release. So does `system-skill-advisor` (v0.18.6.0, v0.18.7.0, v1.0.0.0 and v1.1.0.0). So do `system-skilled-doctor` (v1.1.3.0 to v1.1.7.0) and `system-deep-loop` (v1.6.24.0 to v2.0.2.0). Its modes `deep-research` (v1.15.13.0 to v1.15.15.0) and `deep-review` (v1.11.15.0 to