{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794816524962,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","part":{"id":"prt_1e366c2a20014csJTJ3PLzsKJ6","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","messageID":"msg_1e366b443001N1GfzZdL1nzVgu","type":"step-start","snapshot":"79fdca493a7186b5dfdf09312cfcdcbe87786628"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794816537290,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e366f23d0015LoIXRwqj6pKSk","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","messageID":"msg_1e366b443001N1GfzZdL1nzVgu","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd511bfa24f20169","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"/create:skill\\b\" .skilled/commands .opencode/commands .skilled/agents README.md CONTRIBUTING.md --include=*.md --include=*.txt 2>/dev/null | grep -v \"changelog\\|skill-parent\" | head -20"},"output":"(no output)","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(no output)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \\\"/create:skill\\\\b\\\" .skilled/commands .opencode/commands .skilled/agents README.md CONTRIBUTING.md --include=*.md --include=*.txt 2>/dev/null | grep -v \\\"changelog\\\\|skill-parent\\\" | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794816537149,"end":1794816537290}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794816537389,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e366e95b001X0f3W4uxH6Vh12","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","messageID":"msg_1e366b443001N1GfzZdL1nzVgu","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf96d4ce79fcff08","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"/create:skill\\b\" .skilled/skills/sk-doc --include=*.md --include=*.json --include=*.txt 2>/dev/null | grep -v \"changelog\" | head -30"},"output":".skilled/skills/sk-doc/mode-registry.json:74:      \"command\": \"/create:skill-parent\",\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/feature-catalog/skill-format-conversion/skill-format-check-and-convert.md:38:A conversion refuses a hub candidate rather than guessing. A `mode-registry.json` or `hub-router.json` declaration, a nested packet `SKILL.md`, a `local-` prefixed name, an `agent-` prefixed name, a name that collides with another root and a description past 130 characters each stop the run with its own reason and no write, and the hub refusal prints the `/create:skill-parent` line because hub structure belongs to that command. A skill whose `ROUTER.md` already declares the router skips the move entirely and receives the frontmatter normalization alone, and a run on an already converted skill reports that no conversion is needed.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json:41:          \"sibling\": \"/create:skill-parent\",\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json:48:    \"command\": \"/create:skill-parent\",\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:173:    \"PARENT_HUB\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"parent hub\", \"parent skill\", \"mode packet\", \"mode packets\", \"nested packet\", \"nested workflow packet\", \"mode-registry.json\", \"hub-router.json\", \"hub versus standalone skill class\", \"skill hub\", \"/create:skill-parent\"]},\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md:29:| **sk-create-skill** | Scaffold an OpenCode skill (and, via `sk-create-skill-parent`, a parent hub with nested mode packets) | `sk-create-skill/` | `/create:sk-skill`, `/create:skill-parent` |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/hub-router.json:237:        \"/create:skill-parent\"\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md:37:- You are creating a brand-new skill from scratch. Use `/create:sk-skill` or `/create:skill-parent` directly. See [creation-workflow.md](creation-workflow.md) and [parent-skills-nested-packets.md](../parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md)\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md:42:- `/create:skill-parent` - parent-hub scaffold (`create` or `update`). Argument order is `<skill-name> [create|update] [--modes <m1,m2,...>] [--surfaces <s1,s2,...>] [--path <dir>]`\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md:49:- `/doctor:sk-skill convert <name-or-path>` - conversion for a skill that stays single: it plans, waits for your yes, and moves a legacy machine router into the sibling `ROUTER.md`, or stages a plain skill as a new root. It refuses a hub candidate, which it recognises by a hub declaration or a nested packet tree, and a skill that really holds two or more jobs belongs to `/create:skill-parent`\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md:65:| Two or more distinct jobs | Convert to a parent hub (class H) with `/create:skill-parent` |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md:85:`/create:skill-parent` has no convert-in-place flag, so keeping your own single skill is a merge-time choice, not a `/create:*` operation. A skill that stays single does convert in place, and that path is `/doctor:sk-skill convert`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md:102:- `/create:skill-parent` is the scaffold.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md:119:**Failure this prevents:** `/create:skill-parent <name> create` stopping because the folder already exists, or the scaffold overwriting your customized `SKILL.md` and references.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md:121:### Step 3. Scaffold the hub with `/create:skill-parent`\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md:124:@markdown /create:skill-parent <skill-name> create --modes <mode1,mode2,...> [--surfaces <s1,s2,...>] [--path .skilled/skills] [:auto|:confirm]\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md:132:@markdown /create:skill-parent sk-code create --modes quality,review --surfaces acme,opencode\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md:183:That is the scoped generator `/create:skill-parent` already runs. Do not run fleet `ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs --fix` unless you intend to regenerate generated files across every scanned root.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md:197:**Failure this prevents:** shipping a hub that scaffolds but does not pass the same gate `/create:skill-parent` and `/doctor:skill-advisor parent-skill` require.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md:199:If you need another mode later, use `/create:skill-parent <skill-name> update --modes ...`. Do not re-run `create` on the live folder.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md:269:- `.skilled/commands/create/skill-parent.md` - `/create:skill-parent` operations `create` and `update`\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md:100:- `/create:skill-parent` applies the same rule as `parent-skill-check.cjs` check `12b-routing-shape`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md:17:The shared field vocabulary that `/create:sk-skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/doctor:skill-advisor tune`, and `/doctor:skill-advisor parent-skill` all render after touching a skill root, so that scaffolding a skill and diagnosing its advisor state describe the same reality in the same words.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md:116:| Parent `/create:skill-parent` create | Full handoff, H-specific values (`leaf-manifest.json` freshness from the scoped generator this workflow just ran) |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md:117:| Parent `/create:skill-parent` update | Full handoff, H-specific values |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:277:The operator plans the conversion of a declared hub, compares the tree, then plans a fixture that nests a packet with no declaration. Each refusal names its own reason, and the hub refusal ends at the `/create:skill-parent` command line rather than a write.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/manual-testing-playbook/standalone-skill/refuse-a-hub-candidate.md:15:This scenario validates the refusal path of the conversion. A skill that declares a hub, or that nests packet `SKILL.md` files, is a hub candidate. Convert names the reason, writes nothing and points at `/create:skill-parent`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/manual-testing-playbook/standalone-skill/refuse-a-hub-candidate.md:31:- Expected signals: the declared hub prints `HUB_DECLARATION: Hub declaration mode-registry.json is present; conversion does not modify hubs.` and exits 1. The nested-packet fixture, which carries no declaration, prints `NESTED_PACKETS: Nested SKILL.md packets make this a hub candidate.` and exits 1. A `local-` prefixed name prints `RESERVED_PREFIX` and an `agent-` prefixed one prints `PERSONA_PREFIX`, each with no write. The tree listing is byte-identical after each attempt. Through the command, the run ends with `STATUS=FAIL` and the same reason, followed by `Next: /create:skill-parent <the parent skill folder>`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/manual-testing-playbook/standalone-skill/refuse-a-hub-candidate.md:45:| SKL-012 | Refuse a hub candidate | Refuse a declared hub and a nested packet tree with a named reason and no write | `Convert the field-notes skill into the Skilled format. Both of its modes share one folder, so convert them as one skill.` | 1. `bash: ls .skilled/skills/field-notes/mode-registry.json` -> 2. `bash: node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/sk-skill-convert.cjs plan field-notes` -> 3. `bash: git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --porcelain .skilled/skills/field-notes` -> 4. `bash: ls .skilled/skills/field-notes-nested/modes/fixture-mode/SKILL.md` -> 5. `bash: node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/sk-skill-convert.cjs plan field-notes-nested` -> 6. `bash: git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --porcelain .skilled/skills/field-notes-nested` | Step 1: the declaration is present and there is no nested packet. Step 2: `HUB_DECLARATION: Hub declaration mode-registry.json is present; conversion does not modify hubs.`, exit 1. Step 3: no output. Step 4: the second fixture nests a packet and declares no hub. Step 5: `NESTED_PACKETS: Nested SKILL.md packets make this a hub candidate.`, exit 1. Step 6: no output | The prompt, both fixtures, both refusal lines with their exit statuses, the unchanged tree listings and the handoff line the command prints after the refusal | PASS if each candidate prints its own named reason, nothing changes and the hub refusal names `/create:skill-parent`. FAIL if any attempt writes, two cases share one reason, or a hub candidate is converted | 1. When the reason is `NESTED_PACKETS`, find the nested `SKILL.md` and confirm the folder is meant to be a hub. 2. When it is `HUB_DECLARATION`, read the named declaration rather than deleting it. 3. When it is `RESERVED_PREFIX` or `PERSONA_PREFIX`, rename the skill instead of converting it under that name. 4. When a refusal wrote anyway, treat the run as failed and read the backup path before anything else |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/manual-testing-playbook/standalone-skill/refuse-a-hub-candidate.md:66:- **Pass**: every candidate prints its own named reason, nothing changes on disk, the workflow status carries the same reason and the hub refusal names the `/create:skill-parent` line.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/sk-doc/mode-registry.json:74:      \"command\": \"/create:skill-parent\",\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/feature-catalog/skill-format-conversion/skill-format-check-and-convert.md:38:A conversion refuses a hub candidate rather than guessing. A `mode-registry.json` or `hub-router.json` declaration, a nested packet `SKILL.md`, a `local-` prefixed name, an `agent-` prefixed name, a name that collides with another root and a description past 130 characters each stop the run with its own reason and no write, and the hub refusal prints the `/create:skill-parent` line because hub structure belongs to that command. A skill whose `ROUTER.md` already declares the router skips the move entirely and receives the frontmatter normalization alone, and a run on an already converted skill reports that no conversion is needed.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json:41:          \"sibling\": \"/create:skill-parent\",\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json:48:    \"command\": \"/create:skill-parent\",\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:173:    \"PARENT_HUB\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"parent hub\", \"parent skill\", \"mode packet\", \"mode packets\", \"nested packet\", \"nested workflow packet\", \"mode-registry.json\", \"hub-router.json\", \"hub versus standalone skill class\", \"skill hub\", \"/create:skill-parent\"]},\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md:29:| **sk-create-skill** | Scaffold an Open