{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794817114577,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e36fbaa60010p346mRZ3tLs6Y","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","messageID":"msg_1e36f9a7c001HGsLGzyTiHRnOY","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b391728d06024eaa","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n- Reading the merge base as main's tip: since `695f4191d` is both the merge base and the parent main merge, the single net diff exposed every line main held, so a line-presence sweep plus context reads proved the merge-loss question directly (iteration 1).\n- Running the real sk-doc resolver against the regenerated manifest: the compiled route returned the manifest's exact hash and generation, so the one generated value in scope was proved live instead of trusted (iteration 2).","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n- Reading the merge base as main's tip: since `695f4191d` is both the merge base and the parent main merge, the single net diff exposed every line main held, so a line-presence sweep plus context reads proved the merge-loss question directly (iteration 1).","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merge-docs-6/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merge-docs-6/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merge-docs-6/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merge-docs-6/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merge-docs-6/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merge-docs-6/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -55,8 +55,9 @@\n \n <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n - Reading the merge base as main's tip: since `695f4191d` is both the merge base and the parent main merge, the single net diff exposed every line main held, so a line-presence sweep plus context reads proved the merge-loss question directly (iteration 1).\n+- Running the real sk-doc resolver against the regenerated manifest: the compiled route returned the manifest's exact hash and generation, so the one generated value in scope was proved live instead of trusted (iteration 2).\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merge-docs-6/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n- Reading the merge base as main's tip: since `695f4191d` is both the merge base and the parent main merge, the single net diff exposed every line main held, so a line-presence sweep plus context reads proved the merge-loss question directly (iteration 1).\\n- Running the real sk-doc resolver against the regenerated manifest: the compiled route returned the manifest's exact hash and generation, so the one generated value in scope was proved live instead of trusted (iteration 2).\", \"oldString\": \"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n- Reading the merge base as main's tip: since `695f4191d` is both the merge base and the parent main merge, the single net diff exposed every line main held, so a line-presence sweep plus context reads proved the merge-loss question directly (iteration 1).\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merge-docs-6/deep-review-strate