{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794817434046,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e374a1b3001wYumuHlzeiTgzC","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","messageID":"msg_1e3748ff2001l2MngFL3hEpH9D","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a10472ead77d6f1f","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":230,"offset":1816,"path":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml, lines 1816-2045\n1816:   phase_synthesis:\n1817:     purpose: Compile all iteration findings into review/review-report.md\n1818:     steps:\n1819: \n1820:       step_fanout_merge:\n1821:         description: \"Merge N lineage registries with strongest-restriction; bind p0/p1/p2 counts for step_derive_verdict; skip when single-executor\"\n1822:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n1823:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n1824:         command: |\n1825:           node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs \\\n1826:             --loop-type review \\\n1827:             --artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\n1828:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1829:         wait_for_completion: true\n1830:         bind_from_output:\n1831:           p0_count: \"active_p0\"\n1832:           p1_count: \"active_p1\"\n1833:           p2_count: \"active_p2\"\n1834:           failed_required_gate_ids: \"failed_required_gate_ids\"\n1835:           search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n1836: \n1837:       step_hydrate_summary_metrics:\n1838:         action: \"Hydrate summary metrics before synthesis\"\n1839:         read:\n1840:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1841:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1842:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1843:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1844:         read_patterns:\n1845:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n1846:         extract:\n1847:           - iteration_count: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across those logs in stable lineage order; otherwise count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across the root state log. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n1848:           - highest_run: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, take the highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration' in those logs in stable lineage order, else 0; otherwise take the highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration' in the root state log, else 0. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n1849:           - current_iteration: \"max(highest_run, iteration_count) + 1\"\n1850:           - p0_count: \"When step_fanout_merge bound it, keep the merged value; the fan-out verdict reads it. Otherwise the count of open findings in {state_paths.findings_registry} with status active and severity P0, for the pre-synthesis display only.\"\n1851:           - p1_count: \"Same rule as p0_count, for severity P1.\"\n1852:           - p2_count: \"Same rule as p0_count, for severity P2.\"\n1853:           - failed_required_gate_ids: \"When step_fanout_merge bound it, keep the merged value. Otherwise take failedRequiredGateIds from the last line of {state_paths.state_log} with type === 'event' and event === 'terminal_gates', else []. Read the state log, not the registry: the reducer last ran before the stop wrote that row.\"\n1854:           - dimensions_covered: \"List of reviewed dimensions\"\n1855:           - dimension_coverage: \"covered / total\"\n1856:           - ac_coverage_signal: \"For spec-folder targets only: if level is 2+ and acceptance-criteria.md exists and implementation-summary.md is in-progress or later, surface the AC_COVERAGE advisory status; otherwise mark exempt.\"\n1857:           - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records\"\n1858:           - reason: \"Use the latest stop reason if present: read stopReason from the last line of {state_paths.state_log} with type === 'event' and event === 'terminal_gates' when it is newer than the latest stop event, since a manual stop is stored only there; else the frozen default 'converged'. (Must be a member of the STOP_REASONS enum: converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused, maxDurationReached.)\"\n1859: \n1860:       # H-1 verdict derivation: parse findings JSONL, map highest severity to verdict\n1861:       # - PASS: no P0 or P1 findings (P2-only or clean)\n1862:       # - CONDITIONAL: any P1 finding or open search debt (no P0, no failed gate)\n1863:       # - FAIL: any P0 finding, or a required quality gate (evidence, scope, coverage) still failing at the terminal stop\n1864:       # Final line of iteration-NNN.md MUST be exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" / \"Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\" / \"Review verdict: FAIL\"\n1865:       step_derive_verdict:\n1866:         action: \"Derive review verdict from accumulated findings\"\n1867:         note: \"ac_coverage_signal is advisory while the validation rule is INFO/default-off; include it in synthesis traceability, but do not change the exact verdict enum from this signal alone.\"\n1868:         branch_on: \"config.fanout\"\n1869:         if_present:\n1870:           command: |\n1871:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/review-verdict.cjs \\\n1872:               --active-p0 {p0_count} \\\n1873:               --active-p1 {p1_count} \\\n1874:               --active-p2 {p2_count} \\\n1875:               --search-debt {search_debt_count} \\\n1876:               --failed-gate-ids '{failed_required_gate_ids}'\n1877:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1878:           wait_for_completion: true\n1879:           bind_from_output:\n1880:             verdict: \"verdict\"\n1881:             has_advisories: \"has_advisories\"\n1882:             active_p0: \"active_p0\"\n1883:             active_p1: \"active_p1\"\n1884:             active_p2: \"active_p2\"\n1885:             search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n1886:           on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. The values the merge bound are the authority on a fan-out root, so an unreadable bound value must stop the run rather than let a verdict be guessed.\"\n1887:         if_absent:\n1888:           command: |\n1889:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/review-verdict.cjs \\\n1890:               --registry-path \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" \\\n1891:               --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1892:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1893:           wait_for_completion: true\n1894:           bind_from_output:\n1895:             verdict: \"verdict\"\n1896:             has_advisories: \"has_advisories\"\n1897:             active_p0: \"active_p0\"\n1898:             active_p1: \"active_p1\"\n1899:             active_p2: \"active_p2\"\n1900:             search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n1901:           on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. A non-zero exit means the registry or the state log could not be read, so this stop has no verdict yet and none may be assumed.\"\n1902:         outputs:\n1903:           - verdict: \"PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\"\n1904:           - has_advisories: \"Boolean true when verdict is PASS and any active P2 findings exist\"\n1905:           - active_p0: \"Active P0 count the verdict used\"\n1906:           - active_p1: \"Active P1 count the verdict used\"\n1907:           - active_p2: \"Active P2 count the verdict used\"\n1908:           - ac_coverage_signal: \"exempt | disabled | pass | advisory-shortfall\"\n1909:         contract: |\n1910:           Every iteration-NNN.md must end with exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" (or CONDITIONAL or FAIL).\n1911:           Downstream automation parses this final line via exact string match — do not vary the format.\n1912: \n1913:       # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Pre-Synthesis ───\n1914:       gate_pre_synthesis:\n1915:         applies_to: confirm\n1916:         type: approval_gate\n1917:         purpose: \"Show all accumulated findings and get approval to synthesize\"\n1918:         present: |\n1919:           ## Review Loop Complete\n1920: \n1921:           **Total Iterations**: {iteration_count}\n1922:           **Stop Reason**: {reason}\n1923:           **Cumulative Findings**: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n1924:           **Dimension Coverage**: {dimensions_covered} ({dimension_coverage})\n1925:           **Recent Iteration Summary**: {last_3_summaries}\n1926: \n1927:           Review the iteration files in `{state_paths.iteration_dir}/` if you want more detail before synthesis.\n1928: \n1929:           Options:\n1930:           A) Proceed to synthesis (compile review/review-report.md)\n1931:           B) Run more iterations (increase max or focus on specific dimension)\n1932:           C) Cancel (keep iteration files)\n1933:         wait_for: \"User response\"\n1934:         after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n1935:         on_A: { proceed_to: step_read_all_iterations }\n1936:         on_B: { action: \"Increase max_iterations or adjust focus, return to loop. When reason is maxDurationReached, raise maxDurationMinutes in the config too, or the duration check stops the loop again and writes another terminal record\", proceed_to: phase_loop }\n1937:         on_C: { action: \"Cancel synthesis, keep artifacts\", status: \"PARTIAL\" }\n1938: \n1939:       step_read_all_iterations:\n1940:         action: \"Read all iteration files and strategy\"\n1941:         read_pattern: \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n1942:         read_also: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1943: \n1944:       step_build_finding_registry:\n1945:         action: \"Build deduplicated finding registry from all iterations\"\n1946:         algorithm: |\n1947:           1. Extract all findings from iteration JSONL delta files\n1948:           2. Compute content_hash for each finding (emission requirement):\n1949:              content_hash = sha256(file_path + \"\\u001f\" + line_range + \"\\u001f\" + finding_type + \"\\u001f\" + normalized_description_80chars)\n1950:              Normalized description = whitespace-collapsed, lowercased, first 80 chars of the finding description.\n1951:           3. Two-tier dedup:\n1952:              PRIMARY: group by content_hash field\n1953:                - Same content_hash, multiple dimensions → single finding, merged `dimensions: [<all>]` array\n1954:                - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n1955:              FALLBACK (legacy records lacking content_hash): file:line + normalized_title\n1956:                - Same file:line, multiple dimensions → single finding, multiple dimension tags\n1957:                - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n1958:           4. Track finding lifecycle:\n1959:              - status: active | duplicate | upgraded | downgraded | contested | resolved_false_positive\n1960:              - Record first_seen, upgraded_in, previous_severity for severity changes\n1961:              - Record dimensions array reflecting all dimensions that emitted this finding\n1962:           5. Resolve contradictions:\n1963:              - Findings marked contested across iterations → referee pass\n1964:              - Determine final severity and status\n1965:           6. Count only 'active' findings for totals. These totals are narrative only; the counts the report and the closeout use come from step_derive_verdict.\n1966:         outputs:\n1967:           - finding_registry: \"Deduplicated list of all findings with metadata\"\n1968: \n1969:       step_adversarial_selfcheck:\n1970:         action: \"Final adversarial self-check on all P0 and P1 findings\"\n1971:         algorithm: |\n1972:           For each active P0/P1 finding:\n1973:             1. Hunter: Re-verify finding against source code (re-read file:line)\n1974:             2. Skeptic: Challenge severity — is this really P0/P1? Could it be P2?\n1975:             3. Referee: Final call — confirm, downgrade, or mark false_positive\n1976:           Record each confirm, downgrade or false_positive call for the report; it does not change the counts or the verdict, which step_derive_verdict took from the registry.\n1977: \n1978:       step_emit_resource_map:\n1979:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n1980:         action: \"Emit {state_paths.resource_map_output} from converged review deltas unless config.resource_map.emit is false\"\n1981:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n1982:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors --emit-resource-map\"\n1983:         read:\n1984:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1985:           - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n1986:         write:\n1987:           - \"{state_paths.resource_map_output}\"\n1988:         guarantee: \"Reducer skips cleanly when config.resource_map.emit == false and writes a deterministic resource-map when enabled.\"\n1989:         note: \"A fan-out root has no root state log before closeout, so the root reducer would fail on the missing file. Each lineage emits its own map, so the report names the ones that exist at {artifact_dir}/lineages/*/resource-map.md.\"\n1990: \n1991:       step_resource_map_coverage_gate:\n1992:         action: \"If resource_map_present, compute the Resource Map Coverage Gate synthesis inputs; otherwise preserve the skip note\"\n1993:         note: \"Cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md. Report touched entries, untouched entries split into expected-by-scope vs gap, and implementation paths absent from the map. Findings raised here use category resource-map-coverage with severity calibrated to the gate outcome.\"\n1994: \n1995:       step_compile_review_report:\n1996:         action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n1997:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1998:         instructions: |\n1999:           **Zero-iteration stop:** When {state_paths.state_log} holds no line with type \"iteration\" (on a fan-out root, when none of the lineage state logs under {state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/ holds one), the review did not run, and the report says so instead of reporting on work that never happened:\n2000:              - Executive Summary: open with `Review did not run`, state the stop reason and `0 iterations dispatched`, keep the verdict and hasAdvisories bound by step_derive_verdict unchanged, and state that the P0/P1/P2 counts mean not examined rather than clean.\n2001:              - Planning Trigger: state that `/speckit:plan` is not required, and set the Planning Packet to `triggered: false` and `reviewDidNotRun: true` with `remediationWorkstreams: []`, keeping every other required key from section 2 at an empty value.\n2002:              - Next step: name `/deep:review` again with a duration budget or iteration cap that allows at least one pass.\n2003:              - Sections 3 to 8: give each a single line saying the review did not run.\n2004: \n2005:           Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n2006: \n2007:           1. **Executive Summary**\n2008:              - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n2009:              - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n2010:              - P0/P1/P2 counts: {active_p0}, {active_p1}, {active_p2}, the counts the verdict used, stated as such\n2011:              - Self-check outcomes: each finding the adversarial self-check confirmed, downgraded or called a false positive, listed apart from the counts\n2012:              - Review scope summary\n2013:              - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n2014: \n2015:           2. **Planning Trigger**\n2016:              - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n2017:              - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n2018:              - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n2019:              - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n2020: \n2021:           3. **Active Finding Registry**\n2022:              - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n2023:              - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n2024: \n2025:           4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n2026:              - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n2027: \n2028:           5. **Spec Seed**\n2029:              - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n2030: \n2031:           6. **Plan Seed**\n2032:              - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n2033: \n2034:            7. **Traceability Status**\n2035:               - Summarize required core protocols first, then applicable overlay protocols\n2036:               - Include status, evidence, and any unresolved drift per protocol\n2037:               - Include `AC_COVERAGE` status for lifecycle-active spec-folder targets: exempt, disabled, pass, or advisory-shortfall, with covered/total and floor when available\n2038: \n2039:           If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n2040:              - `Entries touched`: count of resource-map paths that appear in applied reports\n2041:              - `Entries not touched`: paths in resource-map not in implementation, labeled `expected-by-scope` or `gap`\n2042:              - `Implementation paths absent from resource-map`: `target_files` in applied reports not on the map\n2043: \n2044:           8. **Deferred Items**\n2045:              - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2046]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml, lines 1816-2045\n1816:   phase_synthesis:\n1817:     purpose: Compile all iteration findings into review/review-report.md\n1818:     steps:\n1819: \n1820:       step_fanout_merge:\n1821:         description: \"Merge N lineage registries with strongest-restriction; bind p0/p1/p2 counts for step_derive_verdict; skip when single-executor\"\n1822:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n1823:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n1824:         command: |\n1825:           node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs \\\n1826:             --loop-type review \\\n1827:             --artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\n1828:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1829:         wait_for_completion: true\n1830:         bind_from_output:\n1831:           p0_count: \"active_p0\"\n1832:           p1_count: \"active_p1\"\n1833:           p2_count: \"active_p2\"\n1834:           failed_required_gate_ids: \"failed_required_gate_ids\"\n1835:           search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n1836: \n1837:       step_hydrate_summary_metrics:\n1838:         action: \"Hydrate summary metrics before synthesis\"\n1839:         read:\n1840:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1841:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1842:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1843:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1844:         read_patterns:\n1845:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n1846:         extract:\n1847:           - iteration_count: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across those logs in stable lineage order; otherwise count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across the root state log. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n1848:           - highest_run: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, take the highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration' in those logs in stable lineage order, else 0; otherwise take the highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration' in the root state log, else 0. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n1849:           - current_iteration: \"max(highest_run, iteration_count) + 1\"\n1850:           - p0_count: \"When step_fanout_merge bound it, keep the merged value; the fan-out verdict reads it. Otherwise the count of open findings in {state_paths.findings_registry} with status active and severity P0, for the pre-synthesis display only.\"\n1851:           - p1_count: \"Same rule as p0_count, for severity P1.\"\n1852:           - p2_count: \"Same rule as p0_count, for severity P2.\"\n1853:           - failed_required_gate_ids: \"When step_fanout_merge bound it, keep the merged value. Otherwise take failedRequiredGateIds from the last line of {state_paths.state_log} with type === 'event' and event === 'terminal_gates', else []. Read the state log, not the registry: the reducer last ran before the stop wrote that row.\"\n1854:           - dimensions_covered: \"List of reviewed dimensions\"\n1855:           - dimension_coverage: \"covered / total\"\n1856:           - ac_coverage_signal: \"For spec-folder targets only: if level is 2+ and acceptance-criteria.md exists and implementation-summary.md is in-progress or later, surface the AC_COVERAGE advisory status; otherwise mark exempt.\"\n1857:           - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records\"\n1858:           - reason: \"Use the latest stop reason if present: read stopReason from the last line of {state_paths.state_log} with type === 'event' and event === 'terminal_gates' when it is newer than the latest stop event, since a manual stop is stored only there; else the frozen default 'converged'. (Must be a member of the STOP_REASONS enum: converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused, maxDurationReached.)\"\n1859: \n1860:       # H-1 verdict derivation: parse findings JSONL, map highest severity to verdict\n1861:       # - PASS: no P0 or P1 findings (P2-only or clean)\n1862:       # - CONDITIONAL: any P1 finding or open search debt (no P0, no failed gate)\n1863:       # - FAIL: any P0 finding, or a required quality gate (evidence, scope, coverage) still failing at the terminal stop\n1864:       # Final line of iteration-NNN.md MUST be exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" / \"Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\" / \"Review verdict: FAIL\"\n1865:       step_derive_verdict:\n1866:         action: \"Derive review verdict from accumulated findings\"\n1867:         note: \"ac_coverage_signal is advisory while the validation rule is INFO/default-off; include it in synthesis traceability, but do not change the exact verdict enum from this signal alone.\"\n1868:         branch_on: \"config.fanout\"\n1869:         if_present:\n1870:           command: |\n1871:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/review-verdict.cjs \\\n1872:               --active-p0 {p0_count} \\\n1873:               --active-p1 {p1_count} \\\n1874:               --active-p2 {p2_count} \\\n1875:               --search-debt {search_debt_count} \\\n1876:               --failed-gate-ids '{failed_required_gate_ids}'\n1877:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1878:           wait_for_completion: true\n1879:           bind_from_output:\n1880:             verdict: \"verdict\"\n1881:             has_advisories: \"has_advisories\"\n1882:             active_p0: \"active_p0\"\n1883:             active_p1: \"active_p1\"\n1884:             active_p2: \"active_p2\"\n1885:             search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n1886:           on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. The values the merge bound are the authority on a fan-out root, so an unreadable bound value must stop the run rather than let a verdict be guessed.\"\n1887:         if_absent:\n1888:           command: |\n1889:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/review-verdict.cjs \\\n1890:               --registry-path \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" \\\n1891:               --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1892:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1893:           wait_for_completion: true\n1894:           bind_from_output:\n1895:             verdict: \"verdict\"\n1896:             has_advisories: \"has_advisories\"\n1897:             active_p0: \"active_p0\"\n1898:             active_p1: \"active_p1\"\n1899:             active_p2: \"active_p2\"\n1900:             search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n1901:           on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. A non-zero exit means the registry or the state log could not be read, so this stop has no verdict yet and none may be assumed.\"\n1902:         outputs:\n1903:           - verdict: \"PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\"\n1904:           - has_advisories: \"Boolean true when verdict is PASS and any active P2 findings exist\"\n1905:           - active_p0: \"Active P0 count the verdict used\"\n1906:           - active_p1: \"Active P1 count the verdict used\"\n1907:           - active_p2: \"Active P2 count the verdict used\"\n1908:           - ac_coverage_signal: \"exempt | disabled | pass | advisory-shortfall\"\n1909:         contract: |\n1910:           Every iteration-NNN.md must end with exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" (or CONDITIONAL or FAIL).\n1911:           Downstream automation parses this final line via exact string match — do not vary the format.\n1912: \n1913:       # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Pre-Synthesis ───\n1914:       gate_pre_synthesis:\n1915:         applies_to: confirm\n1916:         type: approval_gate\n1917:         purpose: \"Show all accumulated findings and get approval to synthesize\"\n1918:         present: |\n1919:           ## Review Loop Complete\n1920: \n1921:           **Total Iterations**: {iteration_count}\n1922:           **Stop Reason**: {reason}\n1923:           **Cumulative Findings**: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n1924:           **Dimension Coverage**: {dimensions_covered} ({dimension_coverage})\n1925:           **Recent Iteration Summary**: {last_3_summaries}\n1926: \n1927:           Review the iteration files in `{state_paths.iteration_dir}/` if you want more detail before synthesis.\n1928: \n1929:           Options:\n1930:           A) Proceed to synthesis (compile review/review-report.md)\n1931:           B) Run more iterations (increase max or focus on specific dimension)\n1932:           C) Cancel (keep iteration files)\n1933:         wait_for: \"User response\"\n1934:         after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n1935:         on_A: { proceed_to: step_read_all_iterations }\n1936:         on_B: { action: \"Increase max_iterations or adjust focus, return to loop. When reason is maxDurationReached, raise maxDurationMinutes in the config too, or the duration check stops the loop again and writes another terminal record\", proceed_to: phase_loop }\n1937:         on_C: { action: \"Cancel synthesis, keep artifacts\", status: \"PARTIAL\" }\n1938: \n1939:       step_read_all_iterations:\n1940:         action: \"Read all iteration files and strategy\"\n1941:         read_pattern: \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n1942:         read_also: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1943: \n1944:       step_build_finding_registry:\n1945:         action: \"Build deduplicated finding registry from all iterations\"\n1946:         algorithm: |\n1947:           1. Extract all findings from iteration JSONL delta files\n1948:           2. Compute content_hash for each finding (emission requirement):\n1949:              content_hash = sha256(file_path + \"\\u001f\" + line_range + \"\\u001f\" + finding_type + \"\\u001f\" + normalized_description_80chars)\n1950:              Normalized description = whitespace-collapsed, lowercased, first 80 chars of the finding description.\n1951:           3. Two-tier dedup:\n1952:              PRIMARY: group by content_hash field\n1953:                - Same content_hash, multiple dimensions → single finding, merged `dimensions: [<all>]` array\n1954:                - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n1955:              FALLBACK (legacy records lacking content_hash): file:line + normalized_title\n1956:                - Same file:line, multiple dimensions → single finding, multiple dimension tags\n1957:                - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n1958:           4. Track finding lifecycle:\n1959:              - status: active | duplicate | upgraded | downgraded | contested | resolved_false_positive\n1960:              - Record first_seen, upgraded_in, previous_severity for severity changes\n1961:              - Record dimensions array reflecting all dimensions that emitted this finding\n1962:           5. Resolve contradictions:\n1963:              - Findings marked contested across iterations → referee pass\n1964:              - Determine final severity and status\n1965:           6. Count only 'active' findings for totals. These totals are narrative only; the counts the report and the closeout use come from step_derive_verdict.\n1966:         outputs:\n1967:           - finding_registry: \"Deduplicated list of all findings with metadata\"\n1968: \n1969:       step_adversarial_selfcheck:\n1970:         action: \"Final adversarial self-check on all P0 and P1 findings\"\n1971:         algorithm: |\n1972:           For each active P0/P1 finding:\n1973:             1. Hunter: Re-verify finding against source code (re-read file:line)\n1974:             2. Skeptic: Challenge severity — is this really P0/P1? Could it be P2?\n1975:             3. Referee: Final call — confirm, downgrade, or mark false_positive\n1976:           Record each confirm, downgrade or false_positive call for the report; it does not change the counts or the verdict, which step_derive_verdict took from the registry.\n1977: \n1978:       step_emit_resource_map:\n1979:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n1980:         action: \"Emit {state_paths.resource_map_output} from converged review deltas unless config.resource_map.emit is false\"\n1981:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n1982:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors --emit-resource-map\"\n1983:         read:\n1984:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1985:           - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n1986:         write:\n1987:           - \"{state_paths.resource_map_output}\"\n1988:         guarantee: \"Reducer skips cleanly when config.resource_map.emit == false and writes a deterministic resource-map when enabled.\"\n1989:         note: \"A fan-out root has no root state log before closeout, so the root reducer would fail on the missing file. Each lineage emits its own map, so the report names the ones that exist at {artifact_dir}/lineages/*/resource-map.md.\"\n1990: \n1991:       step_resource_map_coverage_gate:\n1992:         action: \"If resource_map_present, compute the Resource Map Coverage Gate synthesis inputs; otherwise preserve the skip note\"\n1993:         note: \"Cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md. Report touched entries, untouched entries split into expected-by-scope vs gap, and implementation paths absent from the map. Findings raised here use category resource-map-coverage with severity calibrated to the gate outcome.\"\n1994: \n1995:       step_compile_review_report:\n1996:         action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n1997:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1998:         instructions: |\n1999:           **Zero-iteration stop:** When {state_paths.state_log} holds no line with type \"iteration\" (on a fan-out root, when none of the lineage state logs under {state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/ holds one), the review did not run, and the report says so instead of reporting on work that never happened:\n2000:              - Executive Summary: open with `Review did not run`, state the stop reason and `0 iterations dispatched`, keep the verdict and hasAdvisories bound by step_derive_verdict unchanged, and state that the P0/P1/P2 counts mean not examined rather than clean.\n2001:              - Planning Trigger: state that `/speckit:plan` is not required, and set the Planning Packet to `triggered: false` and `reviewDidNotRun: true` with `remediationWorkstreams: []`, keeping every other required key from section 2 at an empty value.\n2002:              - Next step: name `/deep:review` again with a duration budget or iteration cap that allows at least one pass.\n2003:              - Sections 3 to 8: give each a single line saying the review did not run.\n2004: \n2005:           Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n2006: \n2007:           1. **Executive Summary**\n2008:              - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n2009:              - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n2010:              - P0/P1/P2 counts: {active_p0}, {active_p1}, {active_p2}, the counts the verdict used, stated as such\n2011:              - Self-check outcomes: each finding the adversarial self-check confirmed, downgraded or called a false positive, listed apart from the counts\n2012:              - Review scope summary\n2013:              - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n2014: \n2015:           2. **Planning Trigger**\n2016:              - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n2017:              - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n2018:              - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n2019:              - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n2020: \n2021:           3. **Active Finding Registry**\n2022:              - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n2023:              - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n2024: \n2025:           4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n2026:              - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n2027: \n2028:           5. **Spec Seed**\n2029:              - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n2030: \n2031:           6. **Plan Seed**\n2032:              - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n2033: \n2034:            7. **Traceability Status**\n2035:               - Summarize required core protocols first, then applicable overlay protocols\n2036:               - Include status, evidence, and any unresolved drift per protocol\n2037:               - Include `AC_COVERAGE` status for lifecycle-active spec-folder targets: exempt, disabled, pass, or advisory-shortfall, with covered/total and floor when available\n2038: \n2039:           If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n2040:              - `Entries touched`: count of resource-map paths that appear in applied reports\n2041:              - `Entries not touched`: paths in resource-map not in implementation, labeled `expected-by-scope` or `gap`\n2042:              - `Implementation paths absent from resource-map`: `target_files` in applied reports not on the map\n2043: \n2044:           8. **Deferred Items**\n2045:              - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2046]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\": 230, \"offset\": 1816, \"path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794817434035,"end":1794817434046}}}}
