{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794817530234,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e376193c001bim53gnUEv5X9D","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","messageID":"msg_1e37606af001DGOT0WH6TWWt5t","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bf20cfd3cfe044d","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":80,"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-metadata-5/review-report.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-metadata-5/review-report.md, lines 1-80\n1: # Review Report - docs-metadata lineage, command-surfacing pass five\n2: \n3: ## 1. Executive Summary\n4: \n5: - **Overall verdict: FAIL** — gate-level, not defect-level. No P0 and no P1 finding exists. Eight P2 advisories are active. The FAIL comes from one required terminal quality gate: coverage stability was not achieved before the iteration cap (see section 8).\n6: - **hasAdvisories: false** — the advisory flag applies only to a PASS verdict.\n7: - **Active findings: P0=0, P1=0, P2=8.**\n8: - **Review scope**: 14 files from `review/review-scope-5.txt` whose area is `docs-metadata`, plus the shared documents and code they describe. Reviewed across four iterations: traceability, maintainability, correctness and security.\n9: - **Iterations**: 4 of 4. **Stop reason**: `maxIterationsReached`.\n10: - **Release readiness**: `in-progress`.\n11: - **Operator review focus (verbatim)**: \"Code review pass five of command surfacing. Read review/review-brief-5.txt in the packet first and follow it. Review the files in review/review-scope-5.txt whose area equals your lineage label without its -5 suffix, plus docs that describe them. Each finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input. Check the kill switch and direct-call switch paths, command offers on refusal, question, history or mention, Vibe journal scoring, the doctor hooks-file reading, docs against code, and holdout hygiene. Never open command-prompts.jsonl, holdout-prompts.jsonl or behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl except through jq del(.prompt), and print counts only. Change no code and write only inside your lineage folder.\"\n12: \n13: ### Why the verdict is FAIL\n14: \n15: The review itself is complete for its declared scope: all four configured dimensions have a full iteration, every active finding carries file:line evidence, and every finding sits inside the dispatched review scope. The terminal coverage gate still fails for two recorded reasons:\n16: \n17: - `coverageAge = 0`. The fourth dimension (security) was covered in iteration 4, the same iteration the cap ended the loop, so the required one-pass coverage stabilization never ran.\n18: - The reducer-owned `traceability` block is empty because this lineage's iteration records named the protocol field `protocol` where the reducer reads `protocolId`. The underlying core-protocol checks were executed and are reported in section 7; the gate cannot see them through the registry.\n19: \n20: The first condition is a real config conflict: `maxIterations=4` with four dimensions and a one-pass stabilization requirement cannot satisfy coverage stability. The second is a bookkeeping defect in this lineage's record shape, not a missing check. Both are carried in section 8.\n21: \n22: ## 2. Planning Trigger\n23: \n24: `/speckit:plan` is required for the eight advisory remediations and for the coverage-stability follow-up. The packet below is built from the reducer registry plus the iteration `findingDetails`; no field is inferred from prose.\n25: \n26: ```json\n27: {\n28:   \"triggered\": true,\n29:   \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n30:   \"hasAdvisories\": false,\n31:   \"activeFindings\": [\"DM5-P2-001\", \"DM5-P2-002\", \"DM5-P2-003\", \"DM5-P2-004\", \"DM5-P2-005\", \"DM5-P2-006\", \"DM5-P2-007\", \"DM5-P2-008\"],\n32:   \"remediationWorkstreams\": [\n33:     \"WS-1 Documentation counts and contradictions\",\n34:     \"WS-2 Playbook structure and verdict vocabulary\",\n35:     \"WS-3 Inventory and leaf metadata\",\n36:     \"WS-4 Coverage stabilization and record-shape follow-up\"\n37:   ],\n38:   \"specSeed\": [\n39:     \"State the meaning-match corpus size from the generated bridge file rather than a hand-written count.\",\n40:     \"Define one scenario verdict vocabulary across the persistence contract, the review protocol and the release rule.\",\n41:     \"Make the playbook wave plan and the category table one generated inventory.\",\n42:     \"Add the DSH hook README to the authored leaf scope so the generated manifest and aliases include it.\"\n43:   ],\n44:   \"planSeed\": [\n45:     \"Correct the command-meaning row count and reconcile the create-skill alias sentence.\",\n46:     \"Replace the retired NN__ directory instruction with the live feature-directory naming.\",\n47:     \"Schedule CL-005..CL-010 in Wave 2 until the CL-004 scenario exists.\",\n48:     \"Correct the load-rate and path-count wording in the workflow-measure note.\",\n49:     \"Regenerate or restructure the tests README inventory and name the command-surfacing suites.\",\n50:     \"Add hooks/dsh/README.md to leaf-scopes.json and regenerate leaf-manifest.json and leaf-aliases.json.\",\n51:     \"Run one stabilization pass for coverage, or amend the iteration cap to five for a four-dimension review.\"\n52:   ],\n53:   \"findingClasses\": [\"instance-only\", \"class-of-bug\"],\n54:   \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\n55:     \"changelog: workflow measure\",\n56:     \"changelog: upgrade notes\",\n57:     \"feature catalog: command meaning matching\",\n58:     \"manual testing playbook: inputs\",\n59:     \"manual testing playbook: result persistence\",\n60:     \"manual testing playbook: wave plan\",\n61:     \"tests README: directory tree\",\n62:     \"leaf-manifest.json / leaf-aliases.json / leaf-scopes.json\"\n63:   ],\n64:   \"fixCompletenessRequired\": false\n65: }\n66: ```\n67: \n68: ## 3. Active Finding Registry\n69: \n70: All eight findings are P2, active, and evidenced with file:line. None relies on inference.\n71: \n72: ### DM5-P2-001 — Meaning-match row count is one behind the generated bridge corpus\n73: \n74: - **Dimension**: traceability\n75: - **File**: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:26`\n76: - **Evidence**: the catalog says 46 rows; `command-bridges.generated.json` reports `counts.typescriptActive=47` and 47 entries with a non-empty `embeddingText`.\n77: - **Case**: a maintainer checks whether a newly added row is covered, reads 46, and stops one row short of the served set.\n78: - **Impact**: the catalog understates the semantic-lane corpus by one row.\n79: - **Fix**: derive the count from the generated file, or state 47 and name the added row.\n80: - **Disposition**: active. **Finding class**: instance-only.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 81]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-metadata-5/review-report.md, lines 1-80\n1: # Review Report - docs-metadata lineage, command-surfacing pass five\n2: \n3: ## 1. Executive Summary\n4: \n5: - **Overall verdict: FAIL** — gate-level, not defect-level. No P0 and no P1 finding exists. Eight P2 advisories are active. The FAIL comes from one required terminal quality gate: coverage stability was not achieved before the iteration cap (see section 8).\n6: - **hasAdvisories: false** — the advisory flag applies only to a PASS verdict.\n7: - **Active findings: P0=0, P1=0, P2=8.**\n8: - **Review scope**: 14 files from `review/review-scope-5.txt` whose area is `docs-metadata`, plus the shared documents and code they describe. Reviewed across four iterations: traceability, maintainability, correctness and security.\n9: - **Iterations**: 4 of 4. **Stop reason**: `maxIterationsReached`.\n10: - **Release readiness**: `in-progress`.\n11: - **Operator review focus (verbatim)**: \"Code review pass five of command surfacing. Read review/review-brief-5.txt in the packet first and follow it. Review the files in review/review-scope-5.txt whose area equals your lineage label without its -5 suffix, plus docs that describe them. Each finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input. Check the kill switch and direct-call switch paths, command offers on refusal, question, history or mention, Vibe journal scoring, the doctor hooks-file reading, docs against code, and holdout hygiene. Never open command-prompts.jsonl, holdout-prompts.jsonl or behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl except through jq del(.prompt), and print counts only. Change no code and write only inside your lineage folder.\"\n12: \n13: ### Why the verdict is FAIL\n14: \n15: The review itself is complete for its declared scope: all four configured dimensions have a full iteration, every active finding carries file:line evidence, and every finding sits inside the dispatched review scope. The terminal coverage gate still fails for two recorded reasons:\n16: \n17: - `coverageAge = 0`. The fourth dimension (security) was covered in iteration 4, the same iteration the cap ended the loop, so the required one-pass coverage stabilization never ran.\n18: - The reducer-owned `traceability` block is empty because this lineage's iteration records named the protocol field `protocol` where the reducer reads `protocolId`. The underlying core-protocol checks were executed and are reported in section 7; the gate cannot see them through the registry.\n19: \n20: The first condition is a real config conflict: `maxIterations=4` with four dimensions and a one-pass stabilization requirement cannot satisfy coverage stability. The second is a bookkeeping defect in this lineage's record shape, not a missing check. Both are carried in section 8.\n21: \n22: ## 2. Planning Trigger\n23: \n24: `/speckit:plan` is required for the eight advisory remediations and for the coverage-stability follow-up. The packet below is built from the reducer registry plus the iteration `findingDetails`; no field is inferred from prose.\n25: \n26: ```json\n27: {\n28:   \"triggered\": true,\n29:   \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n30:   \"hasAdvisories\": false,\n31:   \"activeFindings\": [\"DM5-P2-001\", \"DM5-P2-002\", \"DM5-P2-003\", \"DM5-P2-004\", \"DM5-P2-005\", \"DM5-P2-006\", \"DM5-P2-007\", \"DM5-P2-008\"],\n32:   \"remediationWorkstreams\": [\n33:     \"WS-1 Documentation counts and contradictions\",\n34:     \"WS-2 Playbook structure and verdict vocabulary\",\n35:     \"WS-3 Inventory and leaf metadata\",\n36:     \"WS-4 Coverage stabilization and record-shape follow-up\"\n37:   ],\n38:   \"specSeed\": [\n39:     \"State the meaning-match corpus size from the generated bridge file rather than a hand-written count.\",\n40:     \"Define one scenario verdict vocabulary across the persistence contract, the review protocol and the release rule.\",\n41:     \"Make the playbook wave plan and the category table one generated inventory.\",\n42:     \"Add the DSH hook README to the authored leaf scope so the generated manifest and aliases include it.\"\n43:   ],\n44:   \"planSeed\": [\n45:     \"Correct the command-meaning row count and reconcile the create-skill alias sentence.\",\n46:     \"Replace the retired NN__ directory instruction with the live feature-directory naming.\",\n47:     \"Schedule CL-005..CL-010 in Wave 2 until the CL-004 scenario exists.\",\n48:     \"Correct the load-rate and path-count wording in the workflow-measure note.\",\n49:     \"Regenerate or restructure the tests README inventory and name the command-surfacing suites.\",\n50:     \"Add hooks/dsh/README.md to leaf-scopes.json and regenerate leaf-manifest.json and leaf-aliases.json.\",\n51:     \"Run one stabilization pass for coverage, or amend the iteration cap to five for a four-dimension review.\"\n52:   ],\n53:   \"findingClasses\": [\"instance-only\", \"class-of-bug\"],\n54:   \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\n55:     \"changelog: workflow measure\",\n56:     \"changelog: upgrade notes\",\n57:     \"feature catalog: command meaning matching\",\n58:     \"manual testing playbook: inputs\",\n59:     \"manual testing playbook: result persistence\",\n60:     \"manual testing playbook: wave plan\",\n61:     \"tests README: directory tree\",\n62:     \"leaf-manifest.json / leaf-aliases.json / leaf-scopes.json\"\n63:   ],\n64:   \"fixCompletenessRequired\": false\n65: }\n66: ```\n67: \n68: ## 3. Active Finding Registry\n69: \n70: All eight findings are P2, active, and evidenced with file:line. None relies on inference.\n71: \n72: ### DM5-P2-001 — Meaning-match row count is one behind the generated bridge corpus\n73: \n74: - **Dimension**: traceability\n75: - **File**: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:26`\n76: - **Evidence**: the catalog says 46 rows; `command-bridges.generated.json` reports `counts.typescriptActive=47` and 47 entries with a non-empty `embeddingText`.\n77: - **Case**: a maintainer checks whether a newly added row is covered, reads 46, and stops one row short of the served set.\n78: - **Impact**: the catalog understates the semantic-lane corpus by one row.\n79: - **Fix**: derive the count from the generated file, or state 47 and name the added row.\n80: - **Disposition**: active. **Finding class**: instance-only.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 81]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\": 80, \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-metadata-5/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794817530172,"end":1794817530234}}}}
