{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794817593438,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e3764592001Dfn75uTyqUAevh","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea9ffed5hOlqAimuHTWO","messageID":"msg_1e3761d07001nfZH5O4cQf1ezX","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb9c64287e39f54e","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Report - merge-docs lineage, command-surfacing pass six\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n- **Overall verdict: FAIL** — gate-level, not defect-level. No P0 and no P1 finding exists. Two P2 advisories are active. The FAIL comes from one required terminal quality gate: coverage stability was not achieved before the iteration cap (see section 8).\n- **hasAdvisories: false** — the advisory flag applies only to a PASS verdict.\n- **Active findings: P0=0, P1=0, P2=2.**\n- **Review scope**: the twelve files from `review/review-scope-6.txt` whose area is `merge-docs`, plus the code their changed claims name. Reviewed across three iterations: traceability, correctness and security, maintainability.\n- **Iterations**: 3 of 3. **Stop reason**: `maxIterationsReached`.\n- **Release readiness**: `in-progress`.\n- **Operator review focus (verbatim)**: \"Review pass six. First read specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-6.txt and follow it: it names your area by lineage label, the scope file review/review-scope-6.txt, the diff command for each area, the recorded limits not to re-report and the holdout rule. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input. Change no code and write only inside your lineage folder.\"\n\n### Why the verdict is FAIL\n\nThe review itself is complete for its declared scope: all four configured dimensions have a full iteration, both findings carry file:line evidence, and every finding sits inside the dispatched review scope. The terminal coverage gate still fails for one mechanical reason:\n\n- `coverageAge = 0`. Maintainability was first covered in iteration 3, the same iteration the cap ended the loop, so the required one-pass coverage stabilization never ran (`terminal-gates.cjs` reason `coverage-too-young`).\n\nThe config conflict is real: `maxIterations=3` with four dimensions and a one-pass stabilization requirement cannot satisfy coverage stability. The traceability and scope gates pass, and the registry records `traceabilityCovered: true`, so this is not a missing-check false negative. The gate is carried in section 8.\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\n`/speckit:plan` is required for the two advisory remediations and for the coverage-stability follow-up. The packet is built from the reducer registry plus the iteration `findingDetails`; no field is inferred from prose.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"triggered\": true,\n  \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n  \"hasAdvisories\": false,\n  \"activeFindings\": [\"MD6-P2-001\", \"MD6-P2-002\"],\n  \"remediationWorkstreams\": [\n    \"WS-1 Release-note index accuracy\",\n    \"WS-2 README health-record scope\",\n    \"WS-3 Coverage stabilization follow-up\"\n  ],\n  \"specSeed\": [\n    \"Make the v4.0.2.1 closing index name the newest system-spec-kit changelog, or generate the range from the changelog folder.\",\n    \"State the OpenCode exception in the README health-record paragraph, so the durable doc and the release note agree.\"\n  ],\n  \"planSeed\": [\n    \"Extend the system-spec-kit range at .skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md:480 to 2.13.4.0 or add the missing release-note section.\",\n    \"Add one clause to README.md:682 naming the OpenCode plugin as the runtime that writes no health record.\",\n    \"Run one stabilization pass for coverage, or amend a future four-dimension lineage to maxIterations=5.\"\n  ],\n  \"findingClasses\": [\"instance-only\"],\n  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\n    \"release notes: v4.0.2.1 closing index\",\n    \"README: advisor observability\",\n    \"system-spec-kit changelog index\",\n    \"OpenCode plugin delivery path\"\n  ],\n  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": false\n}\n```\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\nBoth findings are P2, active, and evidenced with file:line. Neither relies on inference.\n\n### MD6-P2-001 — The release note's system-spec-kit range stops one version short\n\n- **Dimension**: traceability\n- **File**: `.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md:480`\n- **Evidence**: the paragraph says `system-spec-kit` has entries \"for this release\" from `v2.12.41.0 to v2.13.3.0`; `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md:5` and `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.4.0.md:11` are `2.13.4.0`, and the merge commit added the v2.13.4.0 file when it bumped the skill.\n- **Case**: a reader auditing what v4.0.2.1 contains reads the closing index, sees the sequence end at 2.13.3.0, and never opens v2.13.4.0, so the release-level summary omits the \"no command file named skill.md\" rule the same merge added.\n- **Impact**: the release note understates its own content by one system-spec-kit entry.\n- **Fix**: extend the range to `2.13.4.0`, or add a v4.0.2.2 note that carries the entry.\n- **Disposition**: active. **Finding class**: instance-only.\n- **Scope proof**: `rg -n \"v2\\\\.12\\\\.41\\\\.0 to v2\\\\.13\\\\.[0-9]\\\\.0\"` over the twelve scope files returns only line 480; every other skill range on that line matches its `SKILL.md` version.\n- **Affected surface hints**: `[\"release notes\", \"system-spec-kit changelog index\", \"upgrade checklist\"]`\n\n### MD6-P2-002 — The README promises a health record on every prompt hook without the OpenCode exception\n\n- **Dimension**: traceability\n- **File**: `README.md:682`\n- **Evidence**: the added paragraph says \"Every prompt hook run also writes a small health record\"; only the Claude-family hook calls `persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord` (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:258`), and `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` imports no diagnostics writer. The release note names the exception at `.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md:114`, and the doctor setup contract says \"OpenCode has no prompt hook that writes one\" at `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:59`.\n- **Case**: an OpenCode user reads the README, runs one prompt, then `advisor_status`; the response has no `hookHealth` section because the plugin never wrote a record, so the README's promise does not hold on that runtime.\n- **Impact**: one runtime's observability is overstated in the durable README.\n- **Fix**: add \"except the OpenCode plugin\" or an equivalent clause to the README paragraph.\n- **Disposition**: active. **Finding class**: instance-only.\n- **Scope proof**: `rg -n \"persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord\" .opencode/plugins` returns nothing, while the Claude hook is the only non-test binding; `rg -n \"hookHealth\" .opencode/plugins` also returns nothing.\n- **Affected surface hints**: `[\"README advisor section\", \"OpenCode plugin delivery path\", \"advisor_status observability\"]`\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\n1. **WS-1 Release-note index accuracy** — MD6-P2-001. Extend the range at `.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md:480` to `2.13.4.0`. Optional durable fix: generate the range from the changelog folder so the hand-maintained list cannot drift again.\n2. **WS-2 README health-record scope** — MD6-P2-002. Add the OpenCode exception to `README.md:682`. Keep the release note's existing carve-out; only the README copy is missing it.\n3. **WS-3 Coverage stabilization follow-up** — gate-level only, no finding. Schedule one stabilization pass for this area, or raise a future four-dimension review's `maxIterations` to five. The review content is complete; only the gate clock is short.\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\n- The release-level changelog index should name every system-spec-kit version it carries, including the one added by a merge, or be generated from the changelog directory.\n- The README's advisor observability paragraph should describe the same runtime coverage as the release note, naming the OpenCode plugin as the exception.\n- A four-dimension review with a one-pass stabilization rule needs an iteration cap of at least five; state that relation in the review packet's config guidance.\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\n- Correct `.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md:480` to `v2.12.41.0 to v2.13.4.0` and confirm the v2.13.4.0 entry is linked from the release section.\n- Add the OpenCode exception clause to `README.md:682`, then diff the README paragraph against `.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md:114` for any other missing carve-out.\n- For the next pass over this area, set `maxIterations` to five or accept the coverage gate's mechanical failure at the cap.\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | Merge-loss sweep over the twelve paths found no main-held line dropped; every behavior claim tested in iterations 1-2 resolves to a file:line. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | No `checklist.md` at the packet root; the pass-six brief and scope file are the operative checklist and both were read. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | `.skilled/agents/markdown.md:197,290` name `/create:sk-skill`; the command file exists and the 13 related-resource entry files all resolve. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pass | `.vibe/agents/markdown.toml:1` matches the canonical body line for line; the other runtime agent mirrors carry the rename. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | notApplicable | No feature-catalog claim is touched by the twelve paths. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No manual-testing-playbook claim is touched by the twelve paths. |\n\n**AC_COVERAGE**: exempt. The review target has no `checklist.md` and no `implementation-summary.md`, so the spec-folder lifecycle predicate is not active.\n\n## 8. Deferred Items\n\n- **Coverage stabilization (gate-level FAIL cause).** All four dimensions are covered, but `coverageAge=0` because maintainability landed in iteration 3, the cap iteration. The 3-iteration cap and the one-pass stabilization rule conflict. Recovery: run a fourth pass, or amend a future run's `maxIterations` to five for a four-dimension review.\n- **The hand-maintained release-note index.** MD6-P2-001 is the symptom; the closing paragraph at `.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md:480` lists every skill's range by hand. A generated range would prevent recurrence, but that is a separate tooling change and is not required to close the advisory.\n- **The README/release-note overlap.** MD6-P2-002 exists because both copies describe hook health and only one names the OpenCode exception. Removing either copy is not the fix; the durable README should carry the full exception.\n\n## Dimension Expansion Map\n\n- Completed pivots: 0. Failed pivots: 0. Audited overrides: 0.\n- Swept directions: traceability (merge loss and doc claims), correctness and security (generated policy, CI wiring, privacy and shell-reader behavior), maintainability (references, generated boundaries, duplicate workflow block).\n- No dimension was pivoted; no direction was exhausted as a retry.\n\n## 9. Search Ledger\n\n| ID | Dimension | Direction | Result | Disposition |\n|----|-----------|-----------|--------|-------------|\n| SL-01 | traceability | Per-merge line comparison of main's additions against each merge result | No main-held line dropped in the twelve paths | ruled out |\n| SL-02 | traceability | Every changed doc claim against its code | Two mismatches; the rest hold | findings MD6-P2-001/002 |\n| SL-03 | correctness | Run the real sk-doc compiled-route resolver against the regenerated manifest | Hash and generation match the live snapshot | ruled out |\n| SL-04 | correctness | Workflow path filters and Vibe check ordering | `command-tree-parity.yml` carries the same checks and the install runs before them | ruled out |\n| SL-05 | security | Hook health persistence and schema | Prompt-free record; validator rejects forbidden fields | ruled out |\n| SL-06 | security | Vibe hook-wiring shell reader | Tokenizes only; depth capped; never executes | ruled out |\n| SL-07 | maintainability | Every path named by the changed doc lines | All 13 entry files, the command and the packet path exist | ruled out |\n| SL-08 | maintainability | Duplicated workflow path block and generated boundaries | Copies agree; generated files state or prove their source | ruled out |\n\n## 10. Audit Appendix\n\n- Iterations: 3. Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached`. Terminal gate rows: evidence pass, scope pass, coverage fail (`coverage-too-young`).\n- Convergence script gates at the stop: `convergenceGate` pass (score 0.55), `dimensionCoverageGate` fail (`missing=[]`, `coverageAge=0`, `traceabilityCovered=true`), `p0ResolutionGate` pass, `evidenceDensityGate` pass, `hotspotSaturationGate` fail, `claimAdjudicationGate` pass, `fixCompletenessReplayGate` pass, `candidateCoverageGate` fail, `graphlessFallbackGate` fail.\n- The terminal cap is legal at `maxIterationsReached`; the failed gates are recorded as synthesis evidence, and only coverage is a required terminal gate.\n- State records went through `append-mode-event.cjs` (run open, three iteration records, terminal gates); the reducer ran after every iteration.\n- No review target, config, registry, reducer output, command, skill, agent or mirror was modified. All writes stayed inside `review/lineages/merge-docs-6/`.\n- The coverage graph was not seeded because `upsert.cjs` writes outside the lineage; the reducer and `convergence.cjs` ran on the graphless fallback and reported `graphConvergenceScore: 0` with the registry coverage signals intact.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merge-docs-6/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merge-docs-6/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merge-docs-6/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Review Report - merge-docs lineage, command-surfacing pass six\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n- **Overall verdict: FAIL** — gate-level, not defect-level. No P0 and no P1 finding exists. Two P2 advisories are active. The FAIL comes from one required terminal quality gate: coverage stability was not achieved before the iteration cap (see section 8).\\n- **hasAdvisories: false** — the advisory flag applies only to a PASS verdict.\\n- **Active findings: P0=0, P1=0, P2=2.**\\n- **Review scope**: the twelve files from `review/review-scope-6.txt` whose area is `merge-docs`, plus the code their changed claims name. Reviewed across three iterations: traceability, correctness and security, maintainability.\\n- **Iterations**: 3 of 3. **Stop reason**: `maxIterationsReached`.\\n- **Release readiness**: `in-progress`.\\n- **Operator review focus (verbatim)**: \\\"Review pass six. First read specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-6.txt and follow it: it names your area by lineage label, the scope file review/review-scope-6.txt, the diff command for each area, the recorded limits not to re-report and the holdout rule. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input. Change no code and write only inside your lineage folder.\\\"\\n\\n### Why the verdict is FAIL\\n\\nThe review itself is complete for its declared scope: all four configured dimensions have a full iteration, both findings carry file:line evidence, and every finding sits inside the dispatched review scope. The terminal coverage gate still fails for one mechanical reason:\\n\\n- `coverageAge = 0`. Maintainability was first covered in iteration 3, the same iteration the cap ended the loop, so the required one-pass coverage stabilization never ran (`terminal-gates.cjs` reason `coverage-too-young`).\\n\\nThe config conflict is real: `maxIterations=3` with four dimensions and a one-pass stabilization requirement cannot satisfy coverage stability. The traceability and scope gates pass, and the registry records `traceabilityCovered: true`, so this is not a missing-check false negative. The gate is carried in section 8.\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\n`/speckit:plan` is required for the two advisory remediations and for the coverage-stability follow-up. The packet is built from the reducer registry plus the iteration `findingDetails`; no field is inferred from prose.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"triggered\\\": true,\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"FAIL\\\",\\n  \\\"hasAdvisories\\\": false,\\n  \\\"activeFindings\\\": [\\\"MD6-P2-001\\\", \\\"MD6-P2-002\\\"],\\n  \\\"remediationWorkstreams\\\": [\\n    \\\"WS-1 Release-note index accuracy\\\",\\n    \\\"WS-2 README health-record scope\\\",\\n    \\\"WS-3 Coverage stabilization follow-up\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"specSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"Make the v4.0.2.1 closing index name the newest system-spec-kit changelog, or generate the range from the changelog folder.\\\",\\n    \\\"State the OpenCode exception in the README health-record paragraph, so the durable doc and the release note agree.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"planSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"Extend the system-spec-kit range at .skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md:480 to 2.13.4.0 or add the missing release-note section.\\\",\\n    \\\"Add one clause to README.md:682 naming the OpenCode plugin as the runtime that writes no health record.\\\",\\n    \\\"Run one stabilization pass for coverage, or amend a future four-dimension lineage to maxIterations=5.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"findingClasses\\\": [\\\"instance-only\\\"],\\n  \\\"affectedSurfacesSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"release notes: v4.0.2.1 closing index\\\",\\n    \\\"README: advisor observability\\\",\\n    \\\"system-spec-kit changelog index\\\",\\n    \\\"OpenCode plugin delivery path\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"fixCompletenessRequired\\\": false\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\nBoth findings are P2, active, and evidenced with file:line. Neither relies on inference.\\n\\n### MD6-P2-001 — The release note's system-spec-kit range stops one version short\\n\\n- **Dimension**: traceability\\n- **File**: `.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md:480`\\n- **Evidence**: the paragraph says `system-spec-kit` has entries \\\"for this release\\\" from `v2.12.41.0 to v2.13.3.0`; `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md:5` and `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.4.0.md:11` are `2.13.4.0`, and the merge commit added the v2.13.4.0 file when it bumped the skill.\\n- **Case**: a reader auditing what v4.0.2.1 contains reads the closing index, sees the sequence end at 2.13.3.0, and never opens v2.13.4.0, so the release-level summary omits the \\\"no command file named skill.md\\\" rule the same merge added.\\n- **Impact**: the release note understates its own content by one system-spec-kit entry.\\n- **Fix**: extend the range to `2.13.4.0`, or add a v4.0.2.2 note that carries the entry.\\n- **Disposition**: active. **Finding class**: instance-only.\\n- **Scope proof**: `rg -n \\\"v2\\\\\\\\.12\\\\\\\\.41\\\\\\\\.0 to v2\\\\\\\\.13\\\\\\\\.[0-9]\\\\\\\\.0\\\"` over the twelve scope files returns only line 480; every other skill range on that line matches its `SKILL.md` version.\\n- **Affected surface hints**: `[\\\"release notes\\\", \\\"system-spec-kit changelog index\\\", \\\"upgrade checklist\\\"]`\\n\\n### MD6-P2-002 — The README promises a health record on every prompt hook without the OpenCode exception\\n\\n- **Dimension**: traceability\\n- **File**: `README.md:682`\\n- **Evidence**: the added paragraph says \\\"Every prompt hook run also writes a small health record\\\"; only the Claude-family hook calls `persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord` (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:258`), and `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` imports no diagnostics writer. The release note names the exception at `.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md:114`, and the doctor setup contract says \\\"OpenCode has no prompt hook that writes one\\\" at `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:59`.\\n- **Case**: an OpenCode user reads the README, runs one prompt, then `advisor_status`; the response has no `hookHealth` section because the plugin never wrote a record, so the README's promise does not hold on that runtime.\\n- **Impact**: one runtime's observability is overstated in the durable README.\\n- **Fix**: add \\\"except the OpenCode plugin\\\" or an equivalent clause to the README paragraph.\\n- **Disposition**: active. **Finding class**: instance-only.\\n- **Scope proof**: `rg -n \\\"persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord\\\" .opencode/plugins` returns nothing, while the Claude hook is the only non-test binding; `rg -n \\\"hookHealth\\\" .opencode/plugins` also returns nothing.\\n- **Affected surface hints**: `[\\\"README advisor section\\\", \\\"OpenCode plugin delivery path\\\", \\\"advisor_status observability\\\"]`\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\n1. **WS-1 Release-note index accuracy** — MD6-P2-001. Extend the range at `.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md:480` to `2.13.4.0`. Optional durable fix: generate the range from the changelog folder so the hand-maintained list cannot drift again.\\n2. **WS-2 README health-record scope** — MD6-P2-002. Add the OpenCode exception to `README.md:682`. Keep the release note's existing carve-out; only the README copy is missing it.\\n3. **WS-3 Coverage stabilization follow-up** — gate-level only, no finding. Schedule one stabilization pass for this area, or raise a future four-dimension review's `maxIterations` to five. The review content is complete; only the gate clock is short.\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\n- The release-level changelog index should name every system-spec-kit version it carries, including the one added by a merge, or be generated from the changelog directory.\\n- The README's advisor observability paragraph should describe the same runtime coverage as the release note, naming the OpenCode plugin as the exception.\\n- A four-dimension review with a one-pass stabilization rule needs an iteration cap of at least five; state that relation in the review packet's config guidance.\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\n- Correct `.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md:480` to `v2.12.41.0 to v2.13.4.0` and confirm the v2.13.4.0 entry is linked from the release section.\\n- Add the OpenCode exception clause to `README.md:682`, then diff the README paragraph against `.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md:114` for any other missing carve-out.\\n- For the next pass over this area, set `maxIterations` to five or accept the coverage gate's mechanical failure at the cap.\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | Merge-loss sweep over the twelve paths found no main-held line dropped; every behavior claim tested in iterations 1-2 resolves to a file:line. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | No `checklist.md` at the packet root; the pass-six brief and scope file are the operative checklist and both were read. |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | `.skilled/agents/markdown.md:197,290` name `/create:sk-skill`; the command file exists and the 13 related-resource entry files all resolve. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pass | `.vibe/agents/markdown.toml:1` matches the canonical body line for line; the other runtime agent mirrors carry the rename. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | notApplicable | No feature-catalog claim is touched by the twelve paths. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No manual-testing-playbook claim is touched by the twelve paths. |\\n\\n**AC_COVERAGE**: exempt. The review target has no `checklist.md` and no `implementation-summary.md`, so the spec-folder lifecycle predicate is not active.\\n\\n## 8. Deferred Items\\n\\n- **Coverage stabilization (gate-level FAIL cause).** All four dimensions are covered, but `coverageAge=0` because maintainability landed in iteration 3, the cap iteration. The 3-iteration cap and the one-pass stabilization rule conflict. Recovery: run a fourth pass, or amend a future run's `maxIterations` to five for a four-dimension review.\\n- **The hand-maintained release-note index.** MD6-P2-001 is the symptom; the closing paragraph at `.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md:480` lists every skill's range by hand. A generated range would prevent recurrence, but that is a separate tooling change and is not required to close the advisory.\\n- **The README/release-note overlap.** MD6-P2-002 exists because both copies describe hook health and only one names the OpenCode exception. Removing either copy is not the fix; the durable README should carry the full exception.\\n\\n## Dimension Expansion Map\\n\\n- Completed pivots: 0. Failed pivots: 0. Audited overrides: 0.\\n- Swept directions: traceability (merge loss and doc claims), correctness and security (generated policy, CI wiring, privacy and shell-reader behavior), maintainability (references, generated boundaries, duplicate workflow block).\\n- No dimension was pivoted; no direction was exhausted as a retry.\\n\\n## 9. Search Ledger\\n\\n| ID | Dimension | Direction | Result | Disposition |\\n|----|-----------|-----------|--------|-------------|\\n| SL-01 | traceability | Per-merge line comparison of main's additions against each merge result | No main-held line dropped in the twelve paths | ruled out |\\n| SL-02 | traceability | Every changed doc claim against its code | Two mismatches; the rest hold | findings MD6-P2-001/002 |\\n| SL-03 | correctness | Run the real sk-doc compiled-route resolver against the regenerated manifest | Hash and generation match the live snapshot | ruled out |\\n| SL-04 | correctness | Workflow path filters and Vibe check ordering | `command-tree-parity.yml` carries the same checks and the install runs before them | ruled out |\\n| SL-05 | security | Hook health persistence and schema | Prompt-free record; validator rejects forbidden fields | ruled out |\\n| SL-06 | security | Vibe hook-wiring shell reader | Tokenizes only; depth capped; never executes | ruled out |\\n| SL-07 | maintainability | Every path named by the changed doc lines | All 13 entry files, the command and the packet path exist | ruled out |\\n| SL-08 | maintainability | Duplicated workflow path block and generated boundaries | Copies agree; generated files state or prove their source | ruled out |\\n\\n## 10. Audit Appendix\\n\\n- Iterations: 3. Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached`. Terminal gate rows: evidence pass, scope pass, coverage fail (`coverage-too-young`).\\n- Convergence script gates at the stop: `convergenceGate` pass (score 0.55), `dimensionCoverageGate` fail (`missing=[]`, `coverageAge=0`, `traceabilityCovered=true`), `p0ResolutionGate` pass, `evidenceDensityGate` pass, `hotspotSaturationGate` fail, `claimAdjudicationGate` pass, `fixCompletenessReplayGate` pass, `candidateCoverageGate` fail, `graphlessFallbackGate` fail.\\n- The terminal cap is legal at `maxIterationsReached`; the failed gates are recorded as synthesis evidence, and only coverage is a required terminal gate.\\n- State records went through `append-mode-event.cjs` (run open, three iteration records, terminal gates); the reducer ran after every iteration.\\n- No review target, config, registry, reducer output, command, skill, agent or mirror was modified. All writes stayed inside `review/lineages/merge-docs-6/`.\\n- The coverage graph was not seeded because `upsert.cjs` writes outside the lineage; the reducer and `convergence.cjs` ran on the graphless fallback and reported `graphConvergenceScore: 0` with the registry coverage signals intact.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merge-docs-6/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794817541522,"end":1794817593438}}}}
